hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3001","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, Shurayh ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from his father, from Abi Ishaq, from Amir ibn Sad, that Hudhayfah and his father came on the day of Badr, and Abu Jahl and his companions met them and said to them: Perhaps you intend Muhammad. They said: We said: No. He said: He took upon us that we not aid against them. When we came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, we mentioned that to him, and said: O Prophet of Allah, the people took upon us, and if you order us to fight with you we will do. He said: Rather we seek Allah's help and fulfill for them."
"3002","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Marzuban Abi Sad, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Hudhayfah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him on the day of al-Ahzab alone as a detachment."
"3003","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Umar ibn Bazigh narrated to us, al-Harith ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abi Mamar al-Taymi, from Sa'idah ibn Hudhayfah, that Hudhayfah used to say: There is no day more delighting to my eye nor more beloved to myself than a day I come to my family and find with them no food, and they say: We can afford neither little nor much. And he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah guards the believer from the world as the family of the sick guards him from food, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, attends the believer with trial more than a father attends his child with good."
"3004","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Shayban, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Fulfalah al-Jufi, from Hudhayfah, he said: By Allah, had I wished I would narrate to you a thousand words over which you love me, or follow me and believe me, as piety from Allah and His Messenger; and had I wished I would narrate to you a thousand words over which you hate me, avoid me, and belie me."
"3005","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abi Ishaq al-Sabii, from Silah ibn Zufar, he said: Hudhayfah sent one to buy him a shroud, and they bought him a shroud for three hundred dirhams. Then Hudhayfah said: I do not want this, but buy two good white cloths."
"3006","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from his father, from Abi Ishaq, that Silah ibn Zufar narrated to him that Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman was shrouded in two cloths. He said: He sent me and Aba Masud, and we bought him a shroud, a Yemeni embroidered suit for three hundred dirhams. He said: Show me what you bought for me. We showed him, and he said: This is not a shroud for me; sufficient for me are two white cloths with no shirt with them, and I will not be left but a little until I attain better than them or worse than them. So we bought him two white cloths."
"3007","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, he said: I heard al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah saying: We asked Aba Masud: What did Hudhayfah say at death? He said: He said: I seek refuge with Allah from a morning to the Fire; buy me two white cloths and shroud me in them, for they will not be left upon me but a little until I am clothed better than them, or stripped of them with swift stripping."
"3008","Al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abdullah ibn Jumay, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah, he said: Nothing prevented me from witnessing Badr except that the polytheists took upon us. He mentioned the hadith."
"3009","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Aswad narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, he said: We said: How did Hudhayfah attain what Abu Bakr nor Umar attained? Silah ibn Zufar said: By Allah, we asked Hudhayfah about that, and he said: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey one night, and we traveled late into the night. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dozed upon his mount, and people said: If we pushed him now and he fell and his neck broke, we would rest from him. When I heard them, I went before them and walked between him and them, reciting a surah of the Quran. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke and said: Who is this? I said: Hudhayfah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Come near. I came near, and he said: Did you hear what these behind you said? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah; and for that I walked between you and them. He said: They are hypocrites, so-and-so and so-and-so and so-and-so."
"3010","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me choice of Hijrah and Nusrah, and I chose Nusrah."
"3011","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Abi Ishaq, from Silah ibn Zufar, from Hudhayfah, he said: The polytheists seized me and my father on the day of Badr, and took upon us a covenant not to aid the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Fulfill for them, and we seek Allah's help against them."
"3012","Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman died in year thirty-six."
"3013","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Hudhayfah died in year thirty-six."
"3014","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Musarrif ibn Amr al-Yami narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, from Silah ibn Zufar, he said: We said to Hudhayfah: How did you know the affair of the hypocrites, while none of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr nor Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, knew it? He said: I was walking behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he slept upon his mount. I heard people among them saying: If we threw him from his mount and his neck broke, we would rest from him. So I walked between them and him, reciting and raising my voice. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke and said: Who is this? I said: Hudhayfah. He said: Who are these? I said: So-and-so and so-and-so, until I counted them. He said: Did you hear what they said? I said: Yes; and for that I walked between you and them. He said: These, so-and-so and so-and-so - until he counted their names - are hypocrites; do not inform anyone."
"3015","Naming of the companions of al-Aqabah: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Habibah, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir, from his father, he said: There was speech between Ammar ibn Yasir and Wadiah ibn Thabit. Wadiah said to Ammar: You are but a slave of Abi Hudhayfah ibn al-Mughirah; you have not yet been freed. Ammar said: How many were the companions of al-Aqabah? He said: Allah knows best. He said: Tell me of your knowledge. Wadiah fell silent, and those present said to him: Tell him what he asked you; Ammar only intended to tell him that he was among them. He said: We used to say they were fourteen men. Then Ammar said: If you were among them, then they are fifteen. Then Wadiah said: Gently, O Aba al-Yaqzan, I adjure you by Allah not to expose me. Then Ammar said: By Allah, I did not name anyone nor will I ever name, but I bear witness that of the fifteen men, twelve of them are at war with Allah and His Messenger in the life of this world and on the day the witnesses stand."
"3016","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Naming of the companions of al-Aqabah: Mutib ibn Qushayr ibn Mulayl of Banu Amr ibn Awf, who witnessed Badr, and he is the one who said: Muhammad promises us the treasures of Kisra and Qaysar, while one of us is not safe over his privy. And he is the one who said: If we had anything of the affair we would not have been killed here. Al-Zubayr said: He is the one against whom al-Zubayr bore witness with this speech. And Wadiah ibn Thabit ibn Amr ibn Awf, and he is the one who said: We were but jesting and playing, and he is the one who said: Why do I see these reciters of ours most desirous in bellies and most cowardly at meeting. And Jidd ibn Abdullah ibn Nabil ibn al-Harith of Banu Amr ibn Awf, and he is the one about whom Jibril, peace be upon him, said: O Muhammad, who is this black one, thick-haired, his eyes as if two brass pots, looking with the eyes of a devil, his liver the liver of a donkey, informing the hypocrites of your news, trailing his dung. And al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Tai, ally of Banu Amr ibn Awf, and he is the one who hastened to the cistern which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade anyone to touch, and drew from it. And Aws ibn Qayzi, of Banu Harithah, and he is the one who said: Our houses are exposed, and he is the grandfather of Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn Qays. And al-Jallas ibn Suwayd ibn al-Samit, of Banu Amr ibn Awf, and it reached us that he repented after that. And Sad ibn Zurarah of Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar, and he is the one who smoked over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was the youngest of them and the most wicked. And Qays ibn Qahd of Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar. And Suwayd and Dais, of Banu Balhubla, of those whom Ibn Ubayy equipped at Tabuk to discourage people. And Qays ibn Amr ibn Sahl, and Zayd ibn al-Lasit, who was of the Jews of Qaynuqa, outwardly showing Islam, with the cheating of Jews and the hypocrisy of hypocrites. And Salamah ibn al-Humam, of Banu Qaynuqa, who outwardly showed Islam."
"3017","And from the musnad of Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Amash narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Maysarah, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, mentioning the Dajjal: Written between his eyes is Kafir, which every Muslim reads."
"3018","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The Quran was sent down upon seven letters."
"3019","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubaydullah al-Umayri narrated to us, (ha). And Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, both said: Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Abi al-Salt, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be over you rulers who lie; whoever believes them in their lie and aids them in their wrong, he is not of me and I am not of him; and whoever does not believe them in their lie and does not aid them in their wrong, he is of me and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Hawd tomorrow, Allah willing."
"3020","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Qatan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The backbiter will not enter Paradise."
"3021","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Sad Abu Ghaylan al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Silah ibn Zufar, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the wicked in his religion, the foolish in his livelihood, will surely enter Paradise; and by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the one whom the Fire scorched for his sin will surely enter Paradise; and by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, Allah will surely forgive on the Day of Resurrection a forgiveness which Iblis will stretch toward hoping it reaches him."
"3022","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (ha), and Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, my grandfather Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb narrated to us, both said: Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Layth, from Abi Ishaq, from Silah ibn Zufar, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Slandering a chaste woman demolishes the work of a hundred years."
"3023","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jumhur ibn Mansur narrated to us, Ismail ibn Mujalid narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Ribi ibn Hirash, he said: I performed Hajj with Hudhayfah, and he sat with Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with them both. Umar said: O companions of Muhammad, which of you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioning fitnah? Hudhayfah said: I. Umar said: You are bold. He said: Bolder than me is one who concealed knowledge. Umar said: How did you hear it? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: In a man's wealth is a trial, and in his wife and child a trial. Umar said: I did not ask about his private trial. Then Hudhayfah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will come to you after me trials like waves of the sea, pushing one another. He raised his hand and said: O Allah, do not let me reach them. Hudhayfah said: Commander of the Faithful, do not fear; between you and them is a closed door. Umar said: Will the door be opened by opening or by breaking? Hudhayfah said: By breaking, then it will never close until the Day of Resurrection. Umar said: That is evil for this ummah."
"3024","Al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi and Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, both said: Abd al-Mumin ibn Ali al-Zafrani narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abi Khalid al-Dalani, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I was given the closing verses of Surat al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne."
"3025","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, (ha). And Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhuyi narrated to us, both said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, both said: Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: I read in the book of my father in his handwriting, and did not hear it from him, from Qatadah, from Abi Mashar, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in my ummah twenty-seven lying impostors, among them four women; and I am the seal of the prophets, there is no prophet after me."
"3026","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, my uncle Sa'id ibn Isa ibn Talid narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Yusuf al-Makki, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, that they were talking about withdrawal, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them and said: You do it? They said: Yes. He said: Do you not know that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not create a soul that He forms but it will be?"
"3027","240 - Hudhayfah ibn Asid Abu Sarihah al-Ghifari, and he is Hudhayfah ibn Asid ibn al-Aws ibn Waqiah ibn Haram ibn Ghifar ibn Mulayl ibn Damrah ibn Bakr ibn Abd Manah ibn Kinanah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Mudrikah ibn Ilyas ibn Mudar ibn Nizar ibn Madd ibn Adnan. Abu al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah from Hudhayfah ibn Asid: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, (ha). And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, (ha). And Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, (ha). And Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Habib narrated to us; Muslim, Ibn Kathir, and Qurrah said: Shubah narrated to us, and Amr ibn Marzuq said: Shubah informed us, from Furat al-Qazzaz, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked upon us from a room and said: What are you saying? What are you mentioning? We said: The Hour. He said: It will not stand until you see ten signs: a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula, the emergence of Yajuj and Majuj, the Dajjal, the Beast, the rising of the sun from its west, the descent of Isa son of Maryam, and a fire emerging from the bottom of Aden moving people, resting with them where they rest at noon, evening with them where they evening, and with a wind casting them into the sea."
"3028","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, (ha). And Umar ibn Jafar al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, both said: al-Masudi narrated to us, from Furat al-Qazzaz, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked upon us while we were discussing the Hour, and said: The Hour will not stand until there are ten signs: the rising of the sun from its west, the Smoke, the Dajjal, the Beast, three sinkings: a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula, the descent of Isa son of Maryam, the opening of Yajuj and Majuj, and a fire emerging from the bottom of Aden driving people to the gathering place."
"3029","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Furat al-Qazzaz narrated to us, from Amir ibn Wathilah, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid al-Ghifari, he said: We were sitting talking in the shade of a room of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we mentioned the Hour, and our voices rose. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked upon us from his room and said: What are you asking about? Or what are you talking about? We said: We mentioned the Hour, and our voices rose. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not stand until before it are ten signs: the rising of the sun from its west, the emergence of the Beast, the emergence of Yajuj and Majuj, the Dajjal, Isa son of Maryam, the Smoke, three sinkings: a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula, and the last of that a fire emerging from Yemen, from the bottom of Aden, driving people to the gathering place."
"3030","Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, Qabisah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, (ha). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, all said: Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Furat al-Qazzaz, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked from a room while we were discussing the Hour, and said: The Hour will not stand until there are ten signs: the Dajjal, the Smoke, the rising of the sun from its west, the Beast of the earth, Yajuj and Majuj, three sinkings: a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula, and a fire emerging from the bottom of Aden Abyan driving people to the gathering place, alighting with them when they alight, and resting at noon with them when they rest at noon."
"3031","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Furat, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Aba al-Tufayl; Hudhayfah ibn Asid, companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me, he said: We were talking in the shade of a room, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked upon us from that room and said: What are you talking about? We said: We talk about the Hour. He said: The Hour will not stand until ten signs emerge: the rising of the sun from its west, the Dajjal, the Smoke, the Beast of the earth, three sinkings: a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula, Yajuj and Majuj will emerge, and a fire will emerge from the bottom of Aden surrounding people, none lagging behind it, driving them to the land of gathering. It stays until they fulfill their needs, then moves with them and moves them on. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Hour will not stand until a fire emerges from Ruman or Rakubah, from which the necks of camels at Busra will be lit."
"3032","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Furat al-Qazzaz narrated to us, from Abi al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid Abi Sarihah al-Ghifari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked upon us from an upper room while we were discussing the Hour, and said: You will see before it ten signs: the Smoke, the Dajjal, the Beast, Yajuj and Majuj, the descent of Isa son of Maryam, the rising of the sun from its west, three sinkings: a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula, and the last of that a fire emerging from Yemen or toward Aden driving people to their gathering place."
"3033","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not stand until ten signs emerge: the rising of the sun from its west, the Smoke, the Dajjal, the Beast, three sinkings: a sinking in the west, a sinking in the east, a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula, the descent of Isa son of Maryam, Yajuj and Majuj, and a fire emerging from the bottom of Aden moving people to the gathering place, leaving none behind it, staying for them. Meaning regarding their needs."
"3034","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Talhah ibn Amr narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Abi Sarihah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The Beast will have three emergences in time: it emerges once in the farthest Yemen until its mention spreads among desert folk, while its mention does not enter the town; then it hides a long time after that; then it emerges another near Makkah, and its mention spreads among desert folk and its mention spreads in Makkah; then it hides a long time; then while people one day are at the greatest of mosques in sanctity to Allah, the best and noblest to Allah, the Sacred Mosque, nothing startles them but the side of the mosque swelling between the Corner and the Station to the door of Banu Makhzum on the right of one exiting the mosque. People scatter from it separately and together, while a group of Muslims holds firm for it, knowing they will never escape Allah. It emerges upon them shaking dust from its head, appears to them, and marks their faces until it leaves them as if brilliant stars. Then it goes in the earth, no seeker reaches it nor does a fleer escape it, until a man stands seeking refuge from it in prayer, and it comes to him saying: O so-and-so, now you pray? He turns his face to it, and it brands him in his face, then goes. People converse in their homes, in their travels, share in wealth, and the disbeliever is known from the believer, until the believer says to the disbeliever: O disbeliever, pay me my due, and until the disbeliever says: O believer, pay me my due."
"3035","Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ata, he said: Ikrimah ibn Khalid narrated to me that Aba al-Tufayl narrated to him that he heard Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The wretched is one wretched in his mother's belly, and the felicitous is one admonished by others. I left him wondering at what I heard until I entered upon Abu Sarihah Hudhayfah ibn Asid al-Ghifari, and I expressed wonder. He said: At what did you wonder? I said: I heard your brother Ibn Masud claiming that the wretched is one wretched in his mother's belly, and that the felicitous is one admonished by others. He said: At which of that did you wonder? I said: Is one wretched without deed? He pointed with his hands to his ears and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these two ears of mine saying: The drop falls in the womb forty nights, then the angel forms over it - I think he said: who creates it - and says: O Lord, male or female? So He makes it male or female. Then he says: O Lord, sound or unsound? So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, makes him sound or unsound. Then he says: O Lord, what is his term? What is his creation? Then he says: O Lord, wretched or felicitous? So Allah, Exalted, makes him wretched or felicitous."
"3036","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Abi Sarihah Hudhayfah ibn Asid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come the wind in which Allah takes the soul of every believer, then the rising of the sun from its west, and it is the sign which Allah mentioned in His Book."
"3037","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, (ha). And Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abi al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The wretched is one wretched in his mother's belly, and the felicitous is one admonished by others. I came to Hudhayfah ibn Asid and said: Do you not wonder at the saying of Ibn Masud? He said: What did he say? He said: The wretched is one wretched in his mother's belly, and the felicitous is one admonished by others. Hudhayfah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When forty-five nights pass over the drop, the angel says: Male or female? Allah, Mighty and Majestic, decrees and the angel writes. Then the angel says: Wretched or felicitous? Allah decrees and the angel writes. He said: Then he says: His provision, term, and deed? He said: Allah decrees and the angel writes. He said: Then the scroll is folded, neither added to nor diminished."
"3038","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The angel enters upon the drop after it settles in the womb forty or forty-five nights, and says: O Lord, wretched or felicitous? Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says and they two write; male or female? Allah says and they two write his affliction, trace, provision, and term. Then the scroll is folded, neither added to nor diminished."
"3039","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Rabiah ibn Kulthum narrated to us, my father Kulthum ibn Jubayr narrated to me, from Abi al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah, he said: Ibn Masud, when he addressed us at Kufah, used to say: The wretched is one wretched in his mother's belly, and the felicitous is one felicitous in his mother's belly. He said: I came to Hudhayfah ibn Asid of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Wonder at the raising of Ibn Umm Abd: The wretched is one wretched in his mother's belly. He said: Hudhayfah said to me: What wonders you of that, O Aba al-Tufayl? Shall I not tell you of this regarding wretchedness? And he raised the hadith: An angel is entrusted with the womb some forty nights; when Allah wills to create what He wills by Allah's permission, he says: O Lord, male or female? Your Lord decrees and the angel writes. Then he says: O Lord, wretched or felicitous? Your Lord decrees and the angel writes. Then he says: O Lord, his term? Your Lord decrees and the angel writes. Then it is folded, neither increased nor decreased."
"3040","Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Azrah ibn Thabit narrated to us, (ha). And Zakariyya al-Saji narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Awn ibn Umarah narrated to us, Azrah ibn Thabit narrated to me, from Yaqub, from Amr ibn Wathilah, he said: I heard Ibn Masud narrating to people in the mosque of Kufah, saying: The wretched is one wretched in his mother's belly, and the felicitous is one admonished by others. I came to Hudhayfah ibn Asid and said: Do you wonder at Ibn Masud; he narrates that the wretched is one wretched in his mother's belly, and that the felicitous is one admonished by others - what is the fault of this child? Hudhayfah said: What did you deny of that? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying many numerous times: When the drop settles in the womb and forty days pass for it - and some of my companions said forty-eight days - the angel of the womb comes and forms his bone, flesh, blood, hair, skin, hearing, and sight. He says: O Lord, male or female? O Lord, wretched or felicitous? Allah, Mighty and Majestic, decrees what He wills and writes. Then he says: O Lord, what is his provision? Allah decrees what He wills and writes. Then it is folded with the scroll, and it is not spread until the Day of Resurrection."
"3041","Ishaq ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ayan narrated to us, Azrah ibn Thabit al-Ansari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Aqil al-Makki narrated to me, he said: I heard Aba al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah saying: I came to Hudhayfah ibn Asid, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When the drop falls in the womb. Then he mentioned the like of it."
"3042","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ubayd ibn Abi Talhah al-Makki, that Aba al-Tufayl al-Bakri informed him that he heard Ibn Masud saying: The wretched is one wretched in his mother's belly, and the felicitous is one admonished by others. I said to him: How is one wretched who did no deed? I met Hudhayfah ibn Asid and informed him of what Ibn Masud said. He said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, wills to create the servant, the angel says: O Lord, male or female? The Lord says what He wills, and the angel writes. Then the angel says: O Lord, wretched or felicitous? The Lord says what He wills and the angel writes. Then he says: O Lord, what will he meet? The Lord says what He wills and the angel writes. Then the angel says: What is his provision? Allah says what He wills and the angel writes. Then he says: O Lord, what is his term? The Lord says what He wills and the angel writes."
"3043","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abi al-Zubayr, that Amir ibn Wathilah narrated to him, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When forty-two nights pass over the drop, Allah sends to it an angel, and he forms it and creates its hearing, sight, skin, flesh, and bone. He says: O Lord, male or female? Your Lord decrees what He wills and the angel writes. Then he says: His provision? Your Lord decrees what He wills and the angel writes, with the scroll in his hand; he neither exceeds what he was ordered nor falls short."
"3044","Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Abi al-Tufayl, that he heard Ibn Masud saying: The wretched is one wretched in his mother's belly, and the felicitous is one admonished by others. I came to Hudhayfah and informed him of the saying of Ibn Masud, and he said: What is denied of this, O son of Wathilah, while I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying it."
"3045","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Sawrah al-Baghdadi, and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, all said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: Pray over a brother of yours who died in other than your land. They said: Who is he? He said: al-Najashi. They prayed over him, and he had done good to those Muslims who fled to him."
"3046","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi, narrated to us Hisham ibn Ammar, narrated to us Shuayb ibn Ishaq, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid: when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of the death of the Negus, he said: Pray over a brother of yours who died outside your land."
"3047","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi. And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi, narrated to us Muhallab ibn al-Ala, narrated to us Shuayb ibn Bayan, narrated to us Imran al-Qattan, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of the death of the Negus, so he said to his Companions: Your brother the Negus has died, so whoever wishes to pray over him let him pray over him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) faced toward Abyssinia and said the takbir over him four times."
"3048","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Yahya ibn Main, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Jafar, narrated to us Shubah, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Zayd ibn Arqam or Hudhayfah ibn Asid: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla."
"3049","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Asfati. And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi, narrated to us Muhallab ibn al-Ala, narrated to us Shuayb ibn Bayan, narrated to us Imran al-Qattan, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever harms the Muslims in their roads, their curse becomes due upon him."
"3050","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani, narrated to us Abu Asim, from Mahdi ibn Maymun, from Uthman ibn Ubayd, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prophethood has gone, so there is no prophethood after me except the mubashshirat. It was said: What are the mubashshirat? He said: The righteous dream which a man sees or which is seen for him."
"3051","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, they said: narrated to us Nasr ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Washsha. And narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari, narrated to us Said ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti, they said: narrated to us Zayd ibn al-Hasan al-Anmati, narrated to us Maruf ibn Kharrabudh, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid al-Ghifari, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from the Farewell Pilgrimage, he forbade his Companions from some clustered trees at al-Batha lest they camp beneath them, then he sent men to them and what was beneath them of thorns was cleared, and he went to them and prayed beneath them, then he stood and said: O people, the Gentle, the All-Aware has informed me that no prophet lived except half the age of the prophet before him, and I think I am about to be called and will answer, and I shall be questioned and you shall be questioned, so what will you say? They said: We bear witness that you conveyed, strove, and advised, so may Allah reward you with good. He said: Do you not bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that His Paradise is true and His Fire is true, and that death is true, and that resurrection after death is true, and that the Hour is coming without doubt, and that Allah will resurrect those in the graves? They said: Yes, we bear witness to that. He said: O Allah, bear witness. Then he said: O people, Allah is my Mawla, and I am the mawla of the believers, and I am closer to them than their own selves, so whomsoever I am his mawla, this one is his mawla - meaning Ali - O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him. Then he said: O people, I am your forerunner, and you will come to me at the Hawd, a basin wider than between Busra and Sanaa, in it silver cups as many as the stars, and I shall ask you when you come to me about the two weighty things, so see how you succeed me in them; the greater weight is the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, a rope one end of which is in the Hand of Allah and one end in your hands, so hold fast to it, do not go astray nor alter; and my household, my family, for the Gentle, the All-Aware informed me that they shall never perish until they come to me at the Hawd."
"3052","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ubulli al-Mufassir, narrated to us Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli, narrated to us Asim ibn Sulayman al-Kuzi, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid: when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the House he said: O Allah, increase this House of Yours in honor, greatness, nobility, righteousness, and awe."
"3053","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Dabbi, narrated to us Yunus ibn Bukayr, from Ziyad ibn al-Mundhir, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah was shown to me last night beside this chamber, so that I know a man among them better than one of you knows his companion. A man among the people said: O Messenger of Allah, those created among them were shown to you; what of those not yet created? He said: They were pictured to me, so by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I know a man among them better than a man knows his companion."
"3054","Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us Uqbah ibn Mukram, narrated to us Abu Bakr al-Hanafi, narrated to us Dawud ibn al-Jarud, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: My ummah was shown to me last night beside this chamber, from its first to its last. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, those created were shown to you, so how were those not created shown to you? He said: They were pictured to me in clay, so that I know a man among them better than one of you knows his companion."
"3055","Al-Shabi from Hudhayfah ibn Asid. Narrated to us Ishaq al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Bayan, from al-Shabi, from Sarayah or Abu Sarayah - Abd al-Razzaq doubted - he said: My family pressed me into neglecting the Sunnah after I knew it; the members of a household used to sacrifice one sheep or two sheep, but now our neighbors make us appear miserly."
"3056","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib, narrated to us Surayj ibn al-Numan, narrated to us Abd al-Malik, from Bayan ibn Bishr, from al-Shabi, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid al-Ghifari, he said: We used to sacrifice a single sacrifice, then people claimed that only stinginess kept us from more, so they pressed us to abandon the Sunnah after we had known it."
"3057","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid, he said: I saw Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, and they would not sacrifice lest it be taken as a binding precedent, so my family pressed me into neglect after I had known the Sunnah, until I now sacrifice on behalf of each one."
"3058","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Asim al-Razi, narrated to us Yahya ibn Nasr ibn Hajib, from Ibn Shubrumah, from al-Shabi, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would bring near two white-flecked rams, then slaughter one of them and say: O Allah, this is on behalf of Muhammad and the household of Muhammad. And he brought the other near and said: O Allah, this is on behalf of my ummah, for whoever bore witness to You of tawhid and bore witness to me of conveyance."
"3059","Al-Rabi ibn Umaylah al-Fazari from Hudhayfah. Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla, narrated to me my father, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from al-Rabi ibn Umaylah, from Abu Sarayah al-Ghifari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ten signs before the Hour: a swallowing in the east, a swallowing in the west, a swallowing in the Hijaz of the Arabs, Gog and Magog, a wind that scatters them and casts them into the sea, the rising of the sun from its west, the Smoke, the Dajjal, the Beast, and the descent of Isa son of Maryam."
"3060","Habib ibn Abi Jammaz from Abu Sarayah. Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Saiqah, narrated to us Ali ibn Thabit al-Dahhan, narrated to us Abu Maryam, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Habib ibn Jammaz and Hilal ibn Abi Zuhayr, from Abu Sarayah, he said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Hour, so he said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared much for it, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: You are with whom you love."
"3061","Hatim ibn Abi Baltaah, a Badri, his kunyah Abu Muhammad, and he was an ally of Banu Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza. Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr: Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah."
"3062","Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed Badr from Banu Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza: Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah, an ally of theirs."
"3063","Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Layth ibn Sad, narrated to us Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: A slave of Hatib came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of Hatib, saying: O Prophet of Allah, Hatib will surely enter the Fire. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You lie; he will not enter it, for he witnessed Badr and al-Hudaybiyah."
"3064","Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, he said: Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah died in the year thirty, his kunyah Abu Muhammad, his age sixty-five; Ibn Affan prayed over him in Madinah."
"3065","And what Hatib narrated. Narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Hashim ibn al-Harith, narrated to us Ubayd Allah ibn Amr, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah, he narrated that his father wrote a letter to the disbelievers of Quraysh while he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and had witnessed Badr. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Ali and al-Zubayr and said: Go until you meet a woman with a letter, then bring it to me. They went until they met her, and said: Give us the letter with you, informing her they would not leave until they stripped every garment off her. She said: Are you not two Muslim men? They said: Yes, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us you have a letter. When she was certain she could not escape them, she loosened the letter from her head and handed it to them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Hatib and read the letter to him, saying: Do you recognize this letter? He said: Yes. He said: What carried you to do that? He said: My children and kin are there, and I was a stranger among you, O company of Quraysh. Umar said: Permit me to kill Hatib. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, for he witnessed Badr, and you do not know; perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do as you wish, I have forgiven you."
"3066","Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Abi Qays, and he is Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Abi Qays ibn Abd Wudd ibn Nadr ibn Malik ibn Hisl ibn Amir ibn Luayy ibn Ghalib ibn Fihr ibn Malik. Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, he said: Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza died, his kunyah Abu Muhammad, in the year fifty-four, his age one hundred and twenty years."
"3067","Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Abi Abbad al-Makki, narrated to us Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar, and Muslim ibn Khalid, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza, he said: We were sitting in the courtyard of the Kaaba in the Jahiliyyah, when a woman came to the House seeking refuge in it from her husband; he stretched his hand toward her and his hand withered, and I saw him in Islam and he was indeed paralyzed in it."
"3068","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr say: Hakim ibn Hizam, Abu Khalid."
"3069","Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, he said: Hakim ibn Hizam died, his kunyah Abu Khalid, in the year fifty-four, and one who says: in the year fifty-eight, and his age one hundred and twenty years; he lived sixty in the Jahiliyyah and sixty in Islam."
"3070","Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, narrated to me Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman, narrated to me my father, he said: Hakim ibn Hizam lived one hundred and twenty years, sixty in Islam and sixty in the Jahiliyyah; and when he swore emphatically he would say: By Him who blessed Hakim that he would be slain on the day... I shall not do such and such; and he would not do it; and his kunyah Abu Khalid."
"3071","Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj, narrated to us Abu Yazid ibn Abi al-Ghimr, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, he said: Hakim ibn Hizam sold a house of his in Makkah to Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, I know it only as for one hundred thousand, and it was said to him: Did you sell your house to him for one hundred thousand? He said: By Allah, I acquired it in the Jahiliyyah only for a wineskin of wine, and bear witness that its price is in the path of Allah."
"3072","Narrated to us Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar al-Makki, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Hamzah, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, from Hakim ibn Hizam: he sold his house to Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, for sixty thousand, and they said: By Allah, Muawiyah has overreached you. He said: I acquired it in the Jahiliyyah only for a wineskin of wine; I call you to witness that it is in the path of Allah, and for the poor and for freeing necks; so which of us is the overreached one?"
"3073","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, narrated to us Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, narrated to us Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman, from Abu Hazim, he said: There was no one in Madinah we heard of who carried more in the path of Allah than Hakim ibn Hizam. He said: Two bedouins came to Madinah asking who carries in the path of Allah, and they were directed to Hakim ibn Hizam, and they came to him among his family and told him what they wanted, and he said to them: Do not hasten until I come out to you. Hakim ibn Hizam would wear clothes brought from Egypt like nets worth four dirhams, take a staff in his hand, and go out with a servant boy of his; and whenever he passed by dunghills or rubbish and saw in them a rag fit for the gear of the camels he carried men upon in the path of Allah, he took it with the tip of his staff and shook it, then said to his two servants: Hold it, you will use it in your gear. One bedouin said to his fellow as he did that: Woe to you, escape with us, for by Allah this man has nothing but picking up chaff. His fellow said: Woe to you, do not hasten until we see. Then he went out with them until he brought them to the market, looked at two great fat pregnant she-camels, bought them and their gear, then said to his servants: Patch with these rags what needs patching of their gear. Then he loaded them with food, wheat and fat, gave them provisions, then gave them the two she-camels. One said to his fellow: By Allah, I have never seen any picker of chaff better than today."
"3074","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya, narrated to us Yahya, narrated to us Abd al-Hamid, he said: I heard Musab ibn Thabit say: By Allah, it has reached me that Hakim ibn Hizam attended the day of Arafah with one hundred necks, one hundred sacrificial camels, and one hundred sheep, and said: All of this is for Allah. So he freed the necks and ordered that slaughtered."
"3075","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I freed forty freedmen in the Jahiliyyah. He said: You entered Islam with what preceded for you."
"3076","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Minjab ibn al-Harith, informed us Ali ibn Mushir, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: Aishah, Hakim ibn Hizam, Shaybah ibn Uthman, and Abd Allah ibn Amir appointed Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr as executor."
"3077","And what Hakim ibn Hizam narrated; Said ibn al-Musayyib from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, and from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Hakim ibn Hizam a grant on the day of Hunayn and he deemed it small, so he increased him, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, which of your two grants is better? He said: The first. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Hakim ibn Hizam, this is green and sweet; whoever takes it with generosity of soul and good appetite, it is blessed for him in it, and whoever takes it with covetousness of soul and bad appetite, it is not blessed for him, and he is like one who eats and is not satisfied, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand. He said: And from you, O Messenger? He said: And from me. He said: By Him who sent you with the truth, I shall never take anything from anyone after you, ever. He said: So he accepted neither register-stipend nor grant until he died; and Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, would say: O Allah, I call You to witness over Hakim ibn Hizam that I invite him to his right from this wealth while he refuses. He said: By Allah, I shall take nothing from you nor from any other. And he died, and he was among the wealthiest of Quraysh."
"3078","Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi, narrated to us Sufyan, narrated to us al-Zuhri, informed me Urwah ibn al-Zubayr and Said ibn al-Musayyib that they heard Hakim ibn Hizam say: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then he said: This wealth is green and sweet; whoever takes it with goodness of soul, it is blessed for him in it, and whoever takes it with covetousness of soul, it is not blessed for him in it, and he is like one who eats and is not satisfied, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand."
"3079","Narrated to us Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Salih, narrated to me al-Layth, narrated to me Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, informed me Urwah ibn al-Zubayr and Ibn al-Musayyib that Hakim ibn Hizam said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then he said: O Hakim, this wealth is green and sweet; whoever takes it with generosity of soul, it is blessed for him in it, and whoever takes it with covetousness of soul, it is not blessed for him in it, like one who eats and is not satisfied, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Him who sent you with the truth, I shall take nothing from anyone after you until I leave the world. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, would invite Hakim to the grant and he would refuse to accept it from him; then Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, invited him to give him, but he refused to accept anything from him, so Umar said: I call you to witness, O company of Muslims, over Hakim ibn Hizam, that I offer him his right apportioned to him from this fay and he refuses to take it. Hakim took nothing from anyone after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he died."
"3080","Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani. And narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib, narrated to us Sad ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, they said: narrated to us Fulayh ibn Sulayman, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for wealth insistently and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, and he said: I do not disapprove of your asking, O Hakim; this wealth is green and sweet, and it is the filth of peoples hands; whoever takes it with generosity is blessed in it, and whoever takes it with covetousness of soul is not blessed in it, and he is like one who eats and is not satisfied; the Hand of Allah is above the hand of the giver, the hand of the giver is above the hand of the receiver, and the hand of the receiver is the lowest of hands."
"3081","Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Salih, narrated to me al-Layth, narrated to me Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr that Hakim ibn Hizam asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for one hundred camels and he gave him, then he asked him for one hundred and he gave him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Hakim ibn Hizam, this wealth is green and sweet; whoever takes it with generosity of soul, it is blessed for him in it, and whoever takes it with covetousness of soul, it is not blessed for him in it, and he is like one who eats and is not satisfied, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support."
"3082","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Rishdin, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Salih, narrated to us Ibn Wahb, informed me Amr ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Shihab that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he gave me, and he mentioned the like of it."
"3083","Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi, narrated to us Sufyan, narrated to us Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father that he heard Hakim ibn Hizam say: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I freed forty freedmen in the Jahiliyyah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You entered Islam with the good that preceded for you."
"3084","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Abdah ibn Sulayman, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what of things I used to do in the Jahiliyyah seeking righteousness thereby? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You entered Islam with the good that preceded. Hisham said: And he had freed slaves in the Jahiliyyah."
"3085","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Hakim ibn Hizam he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what of matters I used to devote myself in during the Jahiliyyah, of freeing and joining kinship - is there reward for me in them? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You entered Islam with the good that preceded for you."
"3086","Narrated to us Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Salih, narrated to me al-Layth, narrated to me Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, informed me Urwah ibn al-Zubayr that Hakim ibn Hizam informed him that he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What of matters I used to devote myself in during the Jahiliyyah - is there anything of them for me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You entered Islam with the good you preceded."
"3087","Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Salih, narrated to me al-Layth, narrated to me Abd al-Rahman ibn Musafir, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr that Hakim ibn Hizam informed him that he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What of matters I used to devote myself in during the Jahiliyyah, of joining kinship, freeing, and charity - is there reward for me in them? Hakim ibn Hizam said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: You entered Islam with the good you preceded."
"3088","Narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad, narrated to me my father, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, informed me Urwah ibn al-Zubayr that Hakim ibn Hizam informed him that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what of matters I used to devote myself in during the Jahiliyyah, of charity or freeing or joining kinship - is there reward in them? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You entered Islam with the good you preceded."
"3089","Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Tawil, narrated to us Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Hakim ibn Hizam that he said: O Messenger of Allah, ruqyas we used to seek healing with, and medicines we used to treat with - do they repel anything of the decree of Allah? He said: They are part of the decree of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"3090","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Abdah ibn Sulayman, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The upper hand is better than the lower hand; let each of you begin with those he supports; the best charity is what is from surplus wealth; whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste; and whoever seeks sufficiency, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will enrich him."
"3091","Narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Said al-Hamdani, narrated to us Ibn Wahb, informed me Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi, and Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Salim, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Hakim ibn Hizam that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The upper hand is better than the lower hand; let each of you begin with those he supports; and the best charity is what is from surplus wealth; whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste; and whoever seeks sufficiency, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will enrich him."
"3092","Narrated to us Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Salih, he said: I read to Anas ibn Iyad: narrated to me Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Hakim ibn Hizam ibn Khuwaylid that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The upper hand is better than the lower hand; let each of you begin with those he supports; and the best charity is from surplus wealth; whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste; and whoever seeks sufficiency, Allah will enrich him."
"3093","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abadah al-Wasiti, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I went out to Yemen and bought the hullah of Dhu Yazan, and I gifted it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the truce period between him and Quraysh, and he said: I do not accept the gift of a mushrik, so he returned it; then I sold it and he bought it and wore it, then he went out to his Companions wearing it, and I never saw anything in anything more beautiful than him in it, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I could not restrain myself from saying so; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard it, turned to me smiling, then entered and clothed Usamah ibn Zayd with it."
"3094","Muslim ibn Jundub from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi, narrated to us Asim ibn Ali, narrated to us Ibn Abi Dhib, from Muslim ibn Jundub, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) insistently, so he said: I do not disapprove of your asking, O Hakim; this wealth is green and sweet, yet with that it is the filth of peoples hands; the Hand of Allah is above the hand of the giver, the hand of the giver is above the hand of the receiver, and the lowest of hands is the hand of the receiver."
"3095","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sayfi from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Abu Asim, from Ibn Jurayj, informed me Ata, from Safwan ibn Mawhab, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sayfi, from Hakim ibn Hizam that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have I not been told - or: have I not been informed - or: has it not reached me - or as Allah willed - that you sell food? I said: Yes. He said: When you buy food, do not sell it until you take full possession of it."
"3096","Yusuf ibn Mahak from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Amr ibn Marzuq, informed us Shubah, from Abu Bishr, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man seeks from me a sale which I do not have; shall I buy it for him? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sell what you do not have."
"3097","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Abu Awanah, from Abu Bishr, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man comes to me wanting a sale from me which I do not have; shall I buy it for him from the market? He said: Do not sell what you do not have."
"3098","Narrated to us Yusuf al-Qadi, narrated to us Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani, narrated to us Hushaym, from Abu Bishr, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man comes to me asking me for a sale I do not have; shall I sell it to him, procuring it for him from the market? He said: Do not sell what you do not have."
"3099","Narrated to us Yusuf al-Qadi, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Harb, narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to sell what I do not have."
"3100","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musafir al-Jawhari and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi, they said: narrated to us Khalid ibn Khidash, narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd, from Yahya ibn Atiq, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to sell what I do not have."
"3101","Narrated to us Yusuf al-Qadi, narrated to us Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ayyub, from Yusuf ibn Mahak that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hakim ibn Hizam: Do not sell what you do not have."
"3102","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hakim ibn Hizam that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sell what you do not have."
"3103","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj, narrated to us Wuhayb, from Ayyub, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to sell what I do not have."
"3104","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Abd al-Warith, from Ayyub, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to sell what I do not have."
"3105","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Abu Usamah, from Shubah, from Abu Bishr, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I would not fall down except standing."
"3106","Abd Allah ibn Ismah from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili, narrated to us Salim ibn Nuh, narrated to us Umar ibn Amir, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Abd Allah ibn Ismah that Hakim ibn Hizam said: O Messenger of Allah, I sell many sales; what of them is lawful for me and what is unlawful for me? He said: Do not sell what you have not taken possession of."
"3107","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah, narrated to us Ubayd Allah ibn Musa, narrated to us Shayban, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Yala ibn Hakim, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Abd Allah ibn Ismah, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who buys these sales and sells them; what of them is lawful for me and what is unlawful for me? He said: Do not sell anything until you take possession of it."
"3108","Hizam ibn Hakim ibn Hizam from his father. Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Jafar al-Wakii al-Misri, narrated to us Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi, narrated to us Ubayd Allah ibn Amr, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Zayd ibn Rufay, from Hizam ibn Hakim ibn Hizam, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the women one day, admonished them, commanded them to fear Allah and obey their husbands and give charity, and said: Some of you will enter Paradise - and he joined his fingers - and most of you are the firewood of Hell - and he separated his fingers. A woman said: Why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Because you curse much, deny the husband, and delay good."
"3109","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad. And narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, they said: narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Ata, from Hizam ibn Hakim ibn Hizam, from his father, he said: I bought some food from the sadaqah-food from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I profited in it before taking possession of it, so I said: I shall not sell it until I ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it, so he said: Do not sell it until you take possession of it."
"3110","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Amr ibn Hisham Abu Umayyah al-Harrani, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Sadaqah, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Hizam ibn Hakim ibn Hizam, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: You have entered a morning in a time of many jurists, few preachers, many givers, few beggars; action in it is better than knowledge; and there will come a time of few jurists, many preachers, many beggars, few givers; knowledge in it is better than action."
"3111","Al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Hizam from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Salih. And narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us Said ibn Yahya. And narrated to us Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar, narrated to us Abu al-Walid: Shub said: narrated to us al-Layth, and Abu al-Walid said: narrated to us Layth ibn Sad, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah, from al-Dahhak ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid ibn Hizam, from Hakim ibn Hizam that he aided with two horses on the day of Hunayn and they were struck, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my two horses have been struck, so compensate me. He gave him, then he asked for more and he gave him more, then he asked for more and he gave him more, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This wealth is green and sweet; whoever asks people, they give him, and the asker is like one who eats and is not satisfied."
"3112","Narrated to us Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas al-Misri, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Ibn Wahb, informed me Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Hizam, from Hakim ibn Hizam that he aided with two horses on the day of Hunayn and they were struck, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My two horses were struck, so compensate me. He gave him, then he asked for more and he gave him more, then he asked for more, then he said: O Hakim, this wealth is green and sweet; whoever asks people, they give him, and the asker therein is like one who eats and is not satisfied."
"3113","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Salih, narrated to us Ibn Wahb, informed me Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr, from al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Hizam that Hakim ibn Hizam: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: This wealth is green and sweet; whoever asks people and they give him, the asker of it is like one who eats and is not satisfied."
"3114","Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar, narrated to us Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi. And narrated to us Yusuf al-Qadi, narrated to us Umar ibn Marzuq. And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz, narrated to us Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi: Abu al-Walid and al-Hawdi said: narrated to us Shubah, and Amr said: informed me Shubah, from Qatadah, from Salih Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two parties to a sale have the option so long as they have not parted; if they are truthful and make clear, their sale is blessed for them, and if they conceal and lie, the blessing of their sale is effaced."
"3115","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz, they said: narrated to us Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi, narrated to us Hammam ibn Yahya, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Hakim ibn Hizam that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two parties to a sale have the option so long as they have not parted - Hammam said: I found in my book he gives choice three times - if they are truthful and make clear, their sale is blessed for them, and if they lie and conceal, they may profit a profit but the blessing of their sale is effaced."
"3116","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar, narrated to us Abu al-Walid. And narrated to us Yusuf al-Qadi, narrated to us Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath, they said: narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two parties to a sale have the option so long as they have not parted."
"3117","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Ismail ibn Ulayyah. And narrated to us Ishaq ibn Khalawayh al-Wasiti, narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, narrated to us Yazid ibn Zuray, they said: narrated to us Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two parties to a sale have the option so long as they have not parted; if they are truthful and make clear, they are blessed, and if they lie and conceal, the blessing of their sale is effaced."
"3118","Narrated to us Muammal ibn Muhammad ibn Sayyar al-Shirazi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Muthanna al-Bahili, narrated to us Salim ibn Nuh, from Umar ibn Amir, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Hakim ibn Hizam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"3119","Musa ibn Talhah from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nuaym, narrated to us Amr ibn Uthman ibn Mawhab, he said: I heard Musa ibn Talhah mention from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is from surplus wealth; the upper hand is better than the lower hand; and begin with those you support."
"3120","Al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani, narrated to us my father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amin, from Hisham ibn Hakim al-Qurashi, from al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a vessel with milk, and to his right was a desert man, and to his left a man among his Companions older than him; when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his need of the drink he said: O youth, this is yours, so will you permit me to give him to drink? He said: Is it mine? He said: Yes. He said: I shall not give my share of your leftover to anyone. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed it to him and he drank."
"3121","Safwan ibn Muhriz al-Mazini from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Faraj. And narrated to us Abd al-Salam ibn Sahl al-Suddi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Azdi, they said: narrated to us Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata, narrated to us Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among his Companions, he said to them: Do you hear what I hear? They said: We hear nothing. He said: I hear the creaking of the heaven, and it is not blamed for creaking, and there is not in it a handspan except upon it an angel prostrating or standing."
"3122","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu Kurayb, narrated to us Uthman ibn Said, from Yazid ibn Ata, from Hurayth ibn Abi Matar, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting, and he said: Fast three days of every month. I said: I am able to do more, until he bargained down with me, then he said: Fast three days of the month. I said: I am able to do more, until he bargained down with me, then he said: Fast the fast of Dawud: fast a day and break a day."
"3123","Al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Hamzah, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to ask him, and he said: Whoever asks people and is given is like one who eats and what he ate does not benefit him; the upper hand is better than the lower hand; the best charity is what is from surplus wealth; and begin with those you support. Hakim said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Him who honored you, I shall never take anything from anyone ever."
"3124","Irak ibn Malik from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Salih, narrated to me al-Layth, narrated to me Abd Allah ibn al-Mughirah, from Irak ibn Malik that Hakim ibn Hizam said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most beloved of men to me in the Jahiliyyah; when he was commissioned as a prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and went out to Madinah, Hakim attended the season while a disbeliever, and found a hullah of Dhu Yazan for sale, bought it to gift it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and came with it to him in Madinah, and offered him to accept it as a gift, but he refused, saying: We do not accept anything from the mushriks, but if you wish I shall take it from you for a price. So I gave it to him when he refused the gift from me, and he wore it, and I saw it on him upon the minbar, and I never saw anything more beautiful than him that day; then he gave it to Usamah ibn Zayd, and Hakim saw it on Usamah and said: O Usamah, do you wear the hullah of Dhu Yazan? He said: Yes; by Allah, I am better than Dhu Yazan, and my father is better than his father. Hakim said: So I went to the people of Makkah marveling at the words of Usamah."
"3125","Ayyub ibn Bashir from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Yusuf, narrated to us Abu Muawiyah. And narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Numayr, they said: narrated to us Hajjaj, from Ibn Shihab, from Ayyub ibn Bashir, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best? He said: Charity to the hostile kindred."
"3126","Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, narrated to us Abbas ibn Abi Shamlah, narrated to me Musa ibn Yaqub, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: We heard a sound from the heaven falling to the earth as if the sound of a pebble in a basin, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw that pebble and we were routed."
"3127","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Mabihamram al-Idhaji, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Asfati, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Yahya al-Shajari, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Musa ibn Yaqub al-Zami, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyan, from Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: On the day of Badr the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded, took a handful of gravel, faced us with it, threw us with it, and said: May the faces be disfigured; so we were routed; then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: And you did not throw when you threw, but Allah threw."
"3128","Abu Salih, freedman of Hakim ibn Hizam, from Hakim. Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abu Salih Abd Allah ibn Salih, narrated to me al-Layth. And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yunus, narrated to us Layth ibn Sad, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu Salih, freedman of Hakim ibn Hizam, from Hakim ibn Hizam that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which charity is best? He said: Begin with those you support, and charity is from surplus wealth."
"3129","Zufar ibn Wathimah from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Hisham ibn Ammar, narrated to us Sadaqah ibn Khalid, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shuaythi, from Zufar ibn Wathimah, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade retaliation to be carried out in the mosques, or poetry to be recited in them, or hudud to be established in them."
"3130","Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman from Hakim. Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib, narrated to us Waki, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shuaythi, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Madani, from Hakim ibn Hizam that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hudud are not established in the mosques, nor is retaliation carried out in them."
"3131","Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Hakim. Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Wahb ibn Baqiyyah, informed us Khalid, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I used to buy food and sell it, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to sell what I do not have."
"3132","Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Shahidi, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Abu Husayn, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Hakim ibn Hizam that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to buy for him a sacrifice for a dinar; he bought it then sold it for two dinars, then bought a sheep for a dinar and came with a dinar; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for him for blessing and commanded him to give the dinar in charity."
"3133","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Waki, from Sufyan, from Abu Husayn, from a man of the people of Madinah, from Hakim ibn Hizam that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to buy for him a sacrifice for a dinar; he bought it then sold it for two dinars, then bought a sheep for a dinar and came with a dinar; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for him for blessing and commanded him to give the dinar in charity."
"3134","Hassan ibn Bilal al-Muzani from Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated to us Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri, narrated to us Ismail ibn Ibrahim, companion of al-Quhi, he said: I heard my father, narrated to us Suwayd Abu Hatim, narrated to us Matar al-Warraq, from Hassan ibn Bilal, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen he said: Do not touch the Quran except in a state of purity."
"3135","Muhammad ibn Sirin from Hakim. Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, and al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani, they said: narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mundhir, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fudayl, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Ibn Sirin, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: Wealth came from Bahrain, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called al-Abbas and scooped for him, saying: Shall I increase you? He said: Yes. So he scooped for him, then said: Shall I increase you? He said: Yes. So he scooped for him, then said: Shall I increase you? He said: Yes. So he scooped for him, then said: Shall I increase you? He said: Yes. He said: Leave for those after you. Then he called me and scooped for me, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, is it good for me or bad for me? He said: No, rather bad for you. So I returned to him what he gave me, then said: No, by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I shall never accept a grant from anyone after you. Muhammad said: Hakim said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to bless me. He said: O Allah, bless the transaction of his hand."
"3136","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib, narrated to us Hawdhah ibn Khalifah, narrated to us Awf, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to sell what I do not have."
"3137","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Ansari al-Asfahani, narrated to us Rawh ibn Isam ibn Yazid, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Sufyan, from Awf, from Ibn Sirin, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me the sale of what I do not have."
"3138","Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Hammad al-Shuaythi, narrated to us Ibn Awn, from Muhammad that Hakim ibn Hizam said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to sell what I do not have."
"3139","Narrated to us Ali, narrated to us Hajjaj. And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil, narrated to us Ali ibn al-Jad, they said: narrated to us al-Rabi ibn Subayh, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to sell what I do not have."
"3140","Narrated to us Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-Attar, narrated to us Talut ibn Abbad, narrated to us Abu Hilal, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me the sale of what I do not have."
"3141","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Mamar ibn Sahl, narrated to us Ubayd Allah ibn Tamam, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I have been blessed in trade; shall I sell a sale then buy it back? He said: No."
"3142","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu Kurayb, narrated to us Yunus ibn Bukayr, from Khalid ibn Dinar, narrated to me Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sell what you do not have."
"3143","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi, narrated to us Isa ibn Yunus al-Ramli, narrated to us Ayyub ibn Suwayd, narrated to me Sufyan al-Thawri, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to sell what I do not have."
"3144","Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, narrated to us Sufyan, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to sell what I do not have."
"3145","Narrated to us Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ismail ibn Sallam al-Wasiti, narrated to us Musa ibn Ismail, narrated to us al-Ala ibn Khalid al-Wasiti, from Mansur ibn Zadham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me four traits in selling: a loan with a sale, two conditions in a sale, selling what you do not have, and profit on what you have not guaranteed."
"3146","Hakim ibn Muawiyah al-Numayri. Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Salih, narrated to me Muawiyah ibn Salih, from al-Safar ibn Nusayr, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, with what did our Lord send you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That you worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, and every Muslim is inviolable from a Muslim; O Hakim ibn Muawiyah, this is your religion; wherever you are, it suffices you."
"3147","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani, narrated to us Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from Muawiyah ibn Hakim, from his uncle Hakim ibn Muawiyah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no bad omen, though blessing may be in the house and the woman."
"3148","Hakim ibn Hazn al-Makhzumi, killed on the day of al-Yamamah. Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those killed on the day of al-Yamamah among the Muslims, then among Quraysh, then among Banu Makhzum: Hakim ibn Hazn ibn Abi Wahb ibn Amr ibn Aidh."
"3149","Al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari, he resided in Basrah, and he is al-Hakam ibn Amr ibn Mujadda ibn Hidhim ibn al-Harith ibn Thalabah ibn Mulayl ibn Damrah ibn Bakr ibn Manah ibn Kinanah. Narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abd Allah ibn al-Samit, he said: Imran ibn al-Husayn said to al-Hakam ibn Amr: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no obedience to anyone in disobedience to Allah? Al-Hakam said: Yes."
"3150","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn al-Taymi, narrated to me Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abd Allah ibn al-Samit, he said: Al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari led the people in prayer on a journey with a sutrah before him, then donkeys passed in front of his companions, so he repeated the prayer with them. They said: He wished to do as al-Walid ibn Uqbah did when he prayed four rakahs of dawn with his companions, then said: Shall I increase you? So I caught up with al-Hakam and mentioned that to him; he stood until the people caught up, and said: I repeated the prayer with you because of the donkeys that passed before you, yet you struck for me the example of Ibn Abi Muayt; I ask Allah to make your conduct good, your reaching good, help you against your enemy, and separate between me and you. So they went and saw in their course only what pleased them; and when they finished, he died."
"3151","And what al-Hakam ibn Amr narrated. Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani. And narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Asim ibn Ali, they said: narrated to us Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Sawadah ibn Asim, from al-Hakam al-Ghifari, and he was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the dubba, the hantam, the muzaffat, and the naqir."
"3152","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Nuaym ibn Hammad, narrated to us Ibn al-Mubarak, from Sulayman al-Taymi. And narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Yahya, from al-Taymi, from Abu Tamimah al-Sulami, from Dulajah ibn Qays that a man said to al-Hakam al-Ghifari: Do you remember the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the naqir, the muqayyar, the dubba, and the hantam? He said: Yes. The other said: And I bear witness to that."
"3153","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Yazid ibn Zuray, narrated to us al-Taymi, from Abu Hajib, from a man of Banu Ghifar among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the naqir, the muqayyar, the dubba, and the hantamah; and he forbade a man to purify himself with the leftover purification-water of a woman."
"3154","Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi. And narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Asim ibn Ali, they said: narrated to us Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Sawadah ibn Asim, from al-Hakam al-Ghifari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the leftover water of a woman."
"3155","Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us al-Rabi ibn Yahya al-Ushnani, narrated to us Shubah, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Hajib, from al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade performing wudu with the leftover of a woman."
"3156","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu Kurayb, narrated to us Waki, from Sufyan, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Hajib, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the leftover water of a woman to perform wudu with."
"3157","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani, narrated to us Mutamir ibn Sulayman, narrated to me Ibn al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari, he said: narrated to me my grandfather, he said: I was with al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari when the messenger of Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, came to him and said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, says: You are the most entitled of those who aided us in this matter. He said: I heard my intimate friend, your cousin, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: When the matter is thus or like this, take a sword of wood; so I have taken a sword of wood."
"3158","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, narrated to us Humayd, Yunus and Habib, from al-Hasan that Ziyad appointed al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari over an army, and Imran ibn Husayn met him in the governors house between the two doors, saying: Do you know why I came to you? Do you remember that when it reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what his commander said to him: Stand and fall into the fire, the man stood to fall into it, was caught and held back, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he fallen into it he would have entered the Fire; there is no obedience in disobedience to Allah? He said: Yes. He said: I only wished to remind you of this hadith."
"3159","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Bazzar al-Tustari, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Shahidi, narrated to us Mutamir ibn Sulayman, from Salm ibn Abi al-Dhayyal, from Muhammad ibn Sirin that Imran ibn Husayn and al-Hakam al-Ghifari - or one of them, and he thought it was Imran - would narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah. He said: Each wished to meet the other for the sake of the hadith, and he met him, saying: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he said: There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah? The other said: Yes. He said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, or as he said."
"3160","Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, they said: narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami, narrated to us Umar ibn Rudayh, narrated to us Hawshab, from al-Hasan, from al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dog, the donkey, and the woman cut off the prayer."
"3161","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Muawiyah al-Jumahi, narrated to us Jamil ibn Ubayd al-Tai, narrated to us Abu al-Mualla, he said: Al-Hakam al-Ghifari said: O plague, take me to you. A man among the people said to him: Why do you say this, when you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Let none of you wish for death? He said: I heard what you heard, but I hasten before six: selling of rule, abundance of police, leadership of boys, shedding of blood, severing of kinship, and a generation in the end of time who take the Quran as flutes."
"3162","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, narrated to us al-Numan ibn Shibl al-Bahili, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Jafar al-Mukharrimi, from Abd al-Karim ibn Suhayb, from Jafar ibn Abd Allah, he said: Al-Hakam - al-Numan said: I think al-Ghifari - saw me eating as a boy from here and here, and said: O my son, do not eat thus; thus eats the devil; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he placed his hand in the bowl or vessel, his fingers did not go beyond the place of his palm."
"3163","Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi, narrated to us Sufyan, narrated to us Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I said to Jabir ibn Zayd: They claim that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys. He said: Al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari used to say that among us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but the Sea refused that - meaning Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them - and he recited: Say: I do not find in what was revealed to me anything forbidden - the verse."
"3164","Al-Hakam ibn Hazn al-Kulafi. Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri, narrated to us Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani. And narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Said ibn Mansur and al-Haytham ibn Kharijah, they said: narrated to us Shihab ibn Khirash ibn Hawshab, narrated to me Shuayb ibn Zurayq al-Tai, he said: I sat with a man who had companionship with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called al-Hakam ibn Hazn al-Kulafi, and he began to narrate, saying: I came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as the seventh of seven or the ninth of nine; permission was sought for us, we entered upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we visited you that you supplicate for us for good; so he supplicated for us for good, ordered us lodged, and ordered for us some dates - and circumstances then were lowly. We stayed some days, attending Friday with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he stood leaning on a bow or staff, praised Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and extolled Him with light, good, blessed words, then said: O people, you will never be able nor do all you are commanded, but be upright and receive glad tidings."
"3165","Al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As ibn Umayyah ibn Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf. Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Qazaah, narrated to us Maslamah ibn Alqamah, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Qays ibn Jubayr, he said: The daughter of al-Hakam said: I said to my grandfather al-Hakam: I never saw a people more incapable nor worse in the affair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than you, O Banu Umayyah. He said: Do not blame us, O my daughter; I narrate to you only what I saw with these two eyes of mine. We said: By Allah, we keep hearing Quraysh exalt this Sabian in our mosque; they appointed a time for him that we might seize him; so we appointed to him, and when we saw him we heard a sound and thought no mountain in Tihamah remained but it crumbled upon us, and we knew nothing until he finished his prayer and returned to his family. Then we appointed another night, and when he came we rose to him, and I saw al-Safa and al-Marwah meet one another, coming between us and him; by Allah, that availed us nothing."
"3166","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Dirar ibn Surad, narrated to us Aidh ibn Habib, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abd Allah al-Madani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, he said: Al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As would sit with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke, he would first twitch; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him and said: You are thus. And he kept twitching until he died."
"3167","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abbad ibn Yaqub, narrated to us Hammad ibn Isa, from Bilal ibn Yahya, from Hudhayfah, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away and Abu Bakr was made caliph, he was spoken to about al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As, and he said: I would never loosen a knot tied by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3168","Al-Hakam ibn Said ibn al-As, killed on the day of Badr as a martyr. Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya al-Abdasi, narrated to us Abu Umayyah ibn Yala al-Taifi, narrated to me my grandfather, from his uncle al-Hakam ibn Said, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge to him, and he said: What is your name? I said: Al-Hakam. He said: Rather you are Abd Allah."
"3169","Al-Hakam ibn al-Harith al-Sulami. Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Abu Kamil al-Jahdari. And narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab, they said: narrated to us Muhammad ibn Humran, narrated to us Atiyyah al-Raa, from al-Hakam ibn al-Harith al-Sulami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me concerning the spoils; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me with my she-camel loosened while I was beating her, and said: Do not beat her. And he said, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Loosen; so she stood and went with the people."
"3170","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Humayd ibn Masadah. And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab, they said: narrated to us Muhammad ibn Humran, from Atiyyah al-Raa, from al-Hakam ibn al-Harith al-Sulami that he campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in three campaigns, he said: He said to us: When you bury me and sprinkle water over my grave, stand over my grave, face the qiblah, and supplicate for me."
"3171","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Sadusi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Humran, narrated to us Atiyyah al-Raa, from al-Hakam ibn al-Harith al-Sulami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes a handspan from the road of the Muslims will come carrying it from seven earths."
"3172","Al-Hakam ibn Kaysan al-Makhzumi, killed on the day of Bir Maunah. Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those killed on the day of Bir Maunah among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Al-Hakam ibn Kaysan al-Makhzumi."
"3173","Al-Hakam ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi. Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar and al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Sufyan ibn al-Hakam or al-Hakam ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he performed wudu would take a handful of water and sprinkle his private part with it."
"3174","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Sallam ibn Abi Muti, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Mujahid, from al-Hakam ibn Sufyan, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinate, take a handful of water, and sprinkle his private part with it."
"3175","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, narrated to us Shubah, informed me Mansur, from Mujahid, from al-Hakam or Abu al-Hakam al-Thaqafi, from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he performed wudu would sprinkle water facing his private part."
"3176","Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Harb, narrated to us Shubah, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from a man of Thaqif called al-Hakam or Abu al-Hakam that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform wudu, then take a handful of water and sprinkle his garments with it."
"3177","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Mualla ibn Asad, narrated to us Wuhayb, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from al-Hakam ibn Sufyan, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinate, perform wudu, take water, and sprinkle with it."
"3178","Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Abu Umar al-Darir, narrated to us Abu Awanah, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from al-Hakam or Abu al-Hakam ibn Sufyan that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated, performed wudu, and sprinkled his private part."
"3179","Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani, narrated to us Sahl ibn Uthman, narrated to us Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, narrated to me my father, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from al-Hakam ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu and took a handful of water and sprinkled his private part with it."
"3180","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Wakii, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam, from Mufaddal ibn Muhalhal, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from al-Hakam ibn Sufyan or Sufyan ibn al-Hakam that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu and sprinkled his private part."
"3181","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bishr, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from al-Hakam ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"3182","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, narrated to us Jubarah ibn Mughallis, narrated to us Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from al-Hakam ibn Sufyan, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform wudu and sprinkle water upon his private part."
"3183","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Jarir, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from al-Hakam or Abu al-Hakam al-Thaqafi, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinate, then call for water, perform wudu, and sprinkle his private part."
"3184","Al-Hakam ibn Umayr al-Thumali. Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi, narrated to us Baqiyyah, from Isa ibn Ibrahim, from Musa ibn Abi Habib, from al-Hakam ibn Umayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you washes, then something appears from his penis, let him perform wudu."
"3185","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi, narrated to us Baqiyyah, from Isa ibn Ibrahim, from Musa ibn Abi Habib, from al-Hakam ibn Umayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Patience and seeking reward, they are the freeing of necks, and Allah admits their doer into Paradise without reckoning."
"3186","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi, narrated to us Baqiyyah, from Isa ibn Ibrahim, from Musa ibn Abi Habib, from his uncle al-Hakam ibn Umayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved of deeds to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is one who feeds a needy person from hunger, or removes a debt from him, or lifts a distress from him."
"3187","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi, narrated to us Baqiyyah, from Isa ibn Ibrahim, from Musa ibn Abi Habib, from al-Hakam ibn Umayr and Aidh ibn Qurz, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not mutilate anything of the creation of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, in which there is a soul."
"3188","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Idris ibn Mutayyib al-Missisi, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, they said: narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Numan al-Farra al-Missisi, narrated to us Yahya ibn Yala al-Aslami, from Musa ibn Abi Habib, from al-Hakam ibn Umayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does you a kindness, recompense him; if you find nothing, supplicate for him."
"3189","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Idris al-Missisi, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, they said: narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Numan al-Farra al-Missisi, narrated to us Yahya ibn Yala al-Aslami, from Musa ibn Abi Habib, from al-Hakam ibn Umayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us: When you stand for prayer, raise your hands, not passing your ears, then say: Allah is Greatest; glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; blessed is Your name; exalted is Your grandeur; and there is no god besides You; and if you add nothing beyond the takbir, it suffices you."
"3190","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Numan al-Farra, narrated to us Yahya ibn Yala, from Musa ibn Abi Habib, from al-Hakam ibn Umayr, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at food, when a man among the people took the servant of the household's towel, took his garment and wiped with it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not wipe with the garment of one you did not clothe."
"3191","Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyya narrated to us, from Isa ibn Ibrahim, from Musa ibn Abi Habib, from al-Hakam ibn Umayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be truly shy of Allah. Guard the head and what it contains, and the belly and what it holds, and remember death and decay. Whoever does that, his reward is the Garden of Refuge."
"3192","Abdous ibn Dayzawayh al-Razi al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Isa ibn Ibrahim, from Musa ibn Abi Habib, from al-Hakam ibn Umayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Quran comes down, and it is the Speech of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"3193","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Baqiyya narrated to us, Isa ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Habib, from al-Hakam ibn Umayr al-Thumali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dreadful matter, the back-breaking burden, and the evil that does not cease is the open display of innovations."
"3194","With this same chain of transmission he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Trim the mustache along with the lips."
"3195","255 - Hajjaj ibn Ilat al-Sulami: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat said: O Messenger of Allah, I have wealth in Mecca and family there, and I want to go to them, so permit me if I speak against you or say something. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him permission to say whatever he wished. He went to his wife when he arrived and said: Gather whatever you have, for I want to buy from the spoils of Muhammad and his Companions, for they have been exposed and their wealth taken. This spread in Mecca, the Muslims were downcast, and the polytheists showed joy. The news reached al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and he was stricken and could not stand, then he sent a servant to al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat: Woe to you, what have you brought, and what are you saying? What Allah has promised is better than what you brought. Al-Hajjaj said: Convey peace to Abu al-Fadl, and tell him to make room for me in one of his houses so I may come to him, for the news is what will please him. His servant came, and when he reached the door he said: Glad tidings, O Abu al-Fadl. Al-Abbas leapt for joy and kissed him between the eyes, and he told him what al-Hajjaj had said, so he freed him. Then al-Hajjaj came to him and told him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had conquered Khaybar and taken their wealth as spoils, and the shares of Allah were distributed in their wealth, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chose Safiyya bint Huyayy for himself and gave her the choice between freeing her and being his wife or rejoining her family, and she chose to be freed and be his wife. But I came for what I had here, wanting to collect it and take it away, so I asked permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he permitted me to say what I wished, so conceal this from me for three days, then mention what you like. His wife gathered her jewelry and goods and gave them to him, and he departed with them. After three days, al-Abbas went to al-Hajjajs wife and asked: What did your husband do? She told him he had left on such-and-such day, and said: May Allah not grieve you, O Abu al-Fadl, what reached you distressed us. He said: Yes, may Allah not grieve me; by praise of Allah it was only what we loved: Allah granted Khaybar to His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chose Safiyya for himself. If you need your husband, join him. She said: I think, by Allah, you are truthful. He said: By Allah I am truthful, and the matter is as I told you. Then he went to the gatherings of Quraysh, and when he passed them they said: Nothing but good befalls you, O Abu al-Fadl. He said: Nothing but good befell me, by praise of Allah; al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat told me that Allah granted Khaybar to His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the shares of Allah were distributed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chose Safiyya for himself. He asked me to conceal it for three days; he only came to take his wealth and what he had here, then leave. So Allah turned the gloom of the Muslims upon the polytheists; the Muslims who had entered their houses downcast came out to al-Abbas, and he told them the news, so the Muslims rejoiced, and Allah returned the gloom, rage, and grief upon the polytheists."
"3196","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Isa ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Uthman Abu Shayba, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: that al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) his sword Dhu al-Fiqar as a gift, and Dihya al-Kalbi gave him his gray mule as a gift."
"3197","256 - Hajjaj ibn Abd Allah al-Nasri: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Makhul: al-Hajjaj ibn Abd Allah al-Nasri narrated to us, saying: Additional spoils are a right; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted additional spoils."
"3198","257 - Hajjaj ibn Malik al-Aslami: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, Ibn Jurayj, and al-Thawri, who said: Hisham ibn Urwa informed us, from his father, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj al-Aslami, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), what removes from me the blame of fosterage? He said: A fine slave or a slave girl."
"3199","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Urwa, from al-Hajjaj, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What removes from me the blame of fosterage? He said: A fine slave or a slave girl."
"3200","Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj al-Aslami, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what removes from me the blame of fosterage? He said: A fine slave or a slave girl."
"3201","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what removes from me the blame of fosterage? He said: A slave or a slave girl at weaning."
"3202","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"3203","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Hafs ibn Maysara narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj: that his father Abu Hadrad asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What removes from me the blame of fosterage? And he mentioned the same."
"3204","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father and Hisham ibn Urwa, from Urwa, from al-Hajjaj ibn Malik al-Aslami, from his father: that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What removes from me the blame of fosterage? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A fine slave or a slave girl."
"3205","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from al-Hajjaj al-Aslami, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what removes from me the blame of fosterage? He said: The fine slave or the slave girl."
"3206","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii narrated to us, Ali ibn Uthman al-Lahiqi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj al-Aslami, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what removes from me the blame of fosterage? He said: A fine slave or a slave girl."
"3207","Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi, and Ibn Saman informed me, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from his father: that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what removes from me the blame of fosterage? He said: The fine slave or the slave girl."
"3208","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Ibn Lahia informed us, from Abu al-Aswad: that he heard Urwa report from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj al-Aslami, from his father: that he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What removes from me the blame of fosterage, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A slave or a slave girl."
"3209","258 - Hajjaj ibn Amr ibn Ghaziyya al-Ansari: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Rafi, from his father, concerning the naming of those who were present with Ali: al-Hajjaj ibn Amr ibn Ghaziyya, and he is the one who used to say in battle: O company of the Ansar, do you want us to say to our Lord when we meet Him: Our Lord, we obeyed our chiefs and our great ones, and they misled us from the path."
"3210","Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us. And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said and Ismail ibn Ulayya narrated to us, all of them from Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Ikrima narrated to me, al-Hajjaj ibn Amr al-Ansari narrated to me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever breaks a bone or becomes lame has exited ihram, and another Hajj is due upon him. He said: So I narrated it to Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayra, and they said: He spoke the truth."
"3211","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar and Yahya narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrima, who said: I heard al-Hajjaj ibn Amr al-Ansari say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever breaks a bone or becomes lame has exited ihram, and a Hajj is due upon him. So I asked Abu Hurayra and Ibn Abbas, and they said: He spoke the truth."
"3212","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrima, from Abd Allah ibn Rafi, the freedman of Umm Salama, who said: I asked al-Hajjaj ibn Amr al-Ansari about the confinement of the pilgrim in ihram, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever breaks a bone, becomes lame, or falls ill has exited ihram, and the Hajj of the coming year is due upon him. Ikrima said: So I asked Abu Hurayra and Ibn Abbas about it, and they said: Al-Hajjaj spoke the truth."
"3213","Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Said ibn Yusuf, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrima: that Abd Allah ibn Rafi, the freedman of Umm Salama, said: I asked al-Hajjaj ibn Amr al-Ansari about one who is detained while in ihram, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever becomes lame, breaks a bone, falls ill, or is detained, let him do the like of it next year, and he has exited ihram. Ikrima said: So I narrated it to Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayra, and they said: He spoke the truth."
"3214","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Jafar ibn Rabia, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Kathir ibn al-Abbas, from al-Hajjaj ibn Amr al-Mazini, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to rise for night prayer after sleeping, and he used to clean his teeth before the night prayer."
"3215","Abu al-Zinba Ruwh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Rabia, from Ibn Hurmuz, from Kathir ibn al-Abbas, from al-Hajjaj ibn Amr ibn Ghaziyya, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: It suffices one of you, when he stands at night praying until morning, that he has kept vigil. Rather, tahajjud is when a man prays after sleeping, then prays after sleeping again; and that was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3216","259 - Hajjaj ibn Amir al-Thumali: Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Thawr, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Abd Allah ibn Amir al-Thumali - and he was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and from al-Hajjaj ibn Amir al-Thumali - and he was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that they both prayed Fajr with Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he recited: When the heaven is split asunder, and he prostrated in it."
"3217","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Shurahbil ibn Muslim, who said: I saw five of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trimming their mustaches, leaving their beards full and dyeing them: Abu Umama al-Bahili, al-Hajjaj ibn Amir al-Thumali, al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Mazini, and Utba ibn Abd al-Sulami. They used to trim along the edge of the lip."
"3218","260 - Hajjaj ibn al-Harith ibn Qays al-Qurashi, then al-Sahmi, killed on the Day of Ajnadayn: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, concerning the naming of those killed on the Day of Ajnadayn among the Muslims, then among Quraysh, then among Banu Sahm: Hajjaj ibn al-Harith ibn Qays."
"3219","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those martyred on the Day of Ajnadayn among Quraysh, then among Banu Sahm: Hajjaj ibn al-Harith ibn Qays."
"3220","Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, concerning the naming of those martyred on the Day of Ajnadayn among Quraysh, then among Banu Sahm: Hajjaj ibn al-Harith."
"3221","261 - Hajjaj al-Bahili: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shuba, who said: I heard al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj al-Bahili narrate from his father - and he had companionship - from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I think it was Abd Allah ibn Masud: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to cool the Zuhr prayer, because the heat is from the blast of Hell."
"3222","Chapter: Those named al-Harith. 262 - Haritha ibn al-Numan al-Ansari, a Badri: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakkai narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, concerning the naming of those present at Badr: Haritha ibn al-Numan ibn Zayd ibn Ubayd ibn Thalaba ibn Ghanm ibn Malik ibn al-Najjar."
"3223","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those present at Badr among the Ansar, then among Banu al-Najjar: Haritha ibn al-Numan, and he is the one who passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was with Jibril, peace be upon him, at al-Maqaid."
"3224","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Haritha ibn al-Numan passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Jibril, peace be upon him, was in private conversation with him, and he did not greet. Jibril, peace be upon him, said: What kept him from greeting? Had he greeted, I would have returned it to him. Then he said: He is indeed among the eighty. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what are the eighty? He said: The people flee from you except eighty; they remain with you, their provision and the provision of their children upon Allah in Paradise. When Haritha returned, he greeted, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why did you not greet when you passed? He said: I saw a man with you, and I disliked interrupting your conversation. He said: Did you see him? He said: Yes. He said: That was Jibril, peace be upon him, and he has spoken. So he informed him of what Jibril, peace be upon him, had said."
"3225","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri: Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabia informed me, from Haritha ibn al-Numan, who said: I passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Jibril, peace be upon him, was sitting with him at al-Maqaid. I greeted him, then passed on. When I left and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned, he said to me: Did you see the one who was with me? I said: Yes. He said: That was Jibril, peace be upon him, and he returned your greeting."
"3226","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Qirmiti al-Adawi narrated to us, Bakr ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Madani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Qays al-Ansari narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Haritha ibn al-Numan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things cling to my nation: superstition, envy, and bad opinion. A man said: What removes them, O Messenger of Allah, from one in whom they are? He said: When you envy, seek Allahs forgiveness; when you suspect, do not verify it; and when you take omens, proceed."
"3227","Masada ibn Sad al-Attar al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us. And Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Walid al-Harawi narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Uthman, from his father, who said: Haritha ibn al-Numan had lost his sight, so he made a string in his prayer place to the door of his room, and placed beside it a basket with dates and other things. When a poor man came and greeted, he would take from that basket, then take hold of the string until he handed it to him. His family would say: We will suffice you. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Handing to the poor wards off an evil death."
"3228","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Umar ibn Abd Allah, the freedman of Ghufra, narrated to us, from Thalaba ibn Abi Malik, from Haritha ibn al-Numan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man goes out with his small flock to the outskirts of the village, attends the prayers, and returns to his family, until when what is around him is eaten and the land becomes hard for him, he says: If only I moved to a hollow with more abundant pasture than this. So he moves, until he attends none of the prayers but Friday. Then when what is around him is eaten and the land becomes hard for him, he says: If only I moved to a hollow with more abundant pasture than this. So he moves, until he attends no Friday and does not know what Friday is, until his heart is sealed."
"3229","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Umar, the freedman of Ghufra. And Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi ibn Yazid and al-Layth ibn Sad informed us, both saying: Umar, the freedman of Ghufra, narrated to us: that Thalaba ibn Abi Malik - and he was elderly, and was the imam of Banu Qurayza until he died - said: I heard Haritha ibn al-Numan say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man goes out with his sheep to the outskirts of the village, attends the prayers, and returns to his family, until when what is around him is eaten and the land becomes hard for him, he says: If only I moved to a hollow with more abundant pasture than this. So he moves, until he attends none of the prayers but Friday. Then when what is around him is eaten and the land becomes hard for him, he says: If only I moved to a hollow with more abundant pasture than this. So he moves, until he attends no Friday and does not know what Friday is, and his heart is sealed."
"3230","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Umar, the freedman of Ghufra, from Thalaba ibn Abi Malik, from Haritha ibn al-Numan, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man may have a small flock at the outskirts of the village. And he mentioned the like of it."
"3231","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, from Umar, the freedman of Ghufra, from Thalaba ibn Abi Malik, from Haritha ibn al-Numan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"3232","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rusta al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim ibn Marzuq al-Razi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Uthman, from his father, from Haritha ibn al-Numan, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Handing to the poor wards off an evil death."
"3233","263 - Haritha ibn al-Rabi al-Ansari, and he is Haritha ibn Suraqa: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that Haritha ibn al-Rabi came as an onlooker on the Day of Uhud, and he was a boy, and a stray arrow struck the hollow of his throat and killed him. His mother al-Rubayyi came and said: O Messenger of Allah, you know the place of Haritha with me; if he is among the people of Paradise, I shall be patient, otherwise you shall see what I do. He said: O mother of Haritha, it is not one Paradise, but many Paradises, and he is in the highest Firdaws. She said: Then I shall be patient."
"3234","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O mother of Haritha, it is a Paradise among Paradises, and Haritha is in the highest Firdaws; so when you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws."
"3235","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Haritha died on the Day of Uhud, struck by an arrow. His mother came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, if he is in Paradise, I shall not weep for him; and if he is in the Fire, Allah shall see what I do. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are Paradises, and he is in the highest Firdaws."
"3236","264 - Haritha ibn Zayd al-Ansari, a Badri: al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those present at Badr among the Ansar, then among Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Haritha ibn Zayd ibn Abi Zuhayr ibn Imri al-Qays."
"3237","265 - Haritha ibn Malik ibn Ghadab ibn Jusham al-Ansari, of Banu Bayada, an Aqabi: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, concerning the naming of the people of al-Aqaba among the Ansar, among Banu Bayada: Haritha ibn Malik ibn Ghadab ibn Jusham."
"3238","266 - Haritha ibn al-Humayyir al-Ashjai, a Badri: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, concerning the naming of those present at Badr among the Ansar, then among Banu Ubayd ibn Adi ibn Ghanm ibn Kab ibn Salama: Haritha ibn al-Humayyir, an ally of theirs from Ashja, of Banu Dahman."
"3239","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those present at Badr among the Ansar, then among Banu Ubayd ibn Adi: Haritha ibn al-Humayyir al-Ashjai, an ally of theirs."
"3240","267 - Haritha ibn Wahb al-Khuzai - Abu Ishaq from Haritha: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Wahb al-Khuzai, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakats in Mina, while the people were at their greatest number."
"3241","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Wahb al-Khuzai: that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the people were at their most secure and most numerous, two rakats in Mina. He said: And I prayed with him at al-Abtah two rakats. Abu Ishaq said: It was said to him: What were you like on that day? He said: On that day I was sharpening arrows and feathering them."
"3242","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, Haritha ibn Wahb al-Khuzai narrated to us - and his mother was under Umar, and she bore Ubayd Allah - who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Mina - while the people were at their greatest number - two rakats in the Farewell Hajj."
"3243","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas and Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us. And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Wahb, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Mina, when the people were at their most secure and most numerous, two rakats."
"3244","Abu Khalifa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Wahb, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he led us in Mina, when we were at our fullest, two rakats."
"3245","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik and Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Wahb al-Khuzai, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Mina two rakats, when the people were at their most secure and most numerous."
"3246","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us. And Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruwasi narrated to us, both saying: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Mina, when the people were at their greatest and most secure, and he prayed two rakats."
"3247","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Wahb, who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Mina two rakats, when the people were at their most secure."
"3248","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from al-Ajlah, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Wahb, who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Mina two rakats, and with Abu Bakr two rakats, and with Umar two rakats, and with Uthman four rakats."
"3249","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Jundayshaburi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, al-Jarrah ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Wahb, who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Mina, when the people were at their greatest and most secure, two rakats."
"3250","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Zibaqi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Dirhami narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Wahb or Wahb ibn Haritha, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Mecca and in Mina two rakats, and with Abu Bakr two rakats, and with Umar two rakats, and with Uthman, in the early part of his caliphate, two rakats."
"3251","Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Malik narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Wahb: that he prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Mina two rakats."
"3252","Ahmad ibn al-Khidr al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abda al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu Muadh al-Nahwi al-Fadl ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Hamza al-Sukkari, from Raqaba ibn Masqala, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Wahb, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Mina two rakats, when the people were at their greatest and most secure."
"3253","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, both saying: Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Wahb, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the Zuhr prayer in Mina, when the people were at their most secure and most numerous, two rakats."
"3254","Mabad ibn Khalid al-Jadali from Haritha: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mabad ibn Khalid, who said: I heard Haritha ibn Wahb say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Shall I not tell you of the people of Paradise? Every weak and downtrodden one; if he swears by Allah, Allah fulfills it. Shall I not tell you of the people of the Fire? Every harsh, coarse, arrogant one."
"3255","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Shadhan narrated to us, my father narrated to us. And Ahmad ibn al-Jarud al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Shadhan narrated to us, Sad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Mabad ibn Khalid, from Haritha ibn Wahb, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise? They said: Yes. He said: A weak, downtrodden man; if he swears by Allah, Allah fulfills it. Shall I not inform you of the people of the Fire? They said: Yes. He said: Every harsh, coarse, arrogant one."
"3256","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhui al-Qadi narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Bakr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, both saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Mabad ibn Khalid, from Haritha ibn Wahb, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not tell you of the people of Paradise? Every weak, downtrodden one; if he swears by Allah, Allah fulfills it. And the people of the Fire are every harsh, arrogant, coarse one."
"3257","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, saying: I found in my grandfathers book in his handwriting: Ismail ibn Aban narrated to us, Misar narrated to me, Mabad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Haritha ibn Wahb and al-Mustawrid al-Fihri, both saying: He said: Shall I not tell you of the people of Paradise? Every weak, downtrodden one; if he swears by Allah, Allah fulfills it. Shall I not tell you of the people of the Fire? Every harsh, coarse, arrogant one."
"3258","Abu Zura Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, both saying: Shuba narrated to us, Mabad ibn Khalid informed me, saying: I heard Haritha ibn Wahb say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Give charity, for there will come upon you a time when a man walks with his charity, and a man says: Had you brought it yesterday I would have accepted it; as for today, I have no need of it."
"3259","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, both saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Mabad ibn Khalid, from Haritha ibn Wahb, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity, for there will come upon you a time when a man walks with his charity and finds none to accept it."
"3260","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, saying: I found in my grandfathers book in his handwriting: Ismail ibn Aban narrated to us, from Misar, from Mabad ibn Khalid, from Haritha ibn Wahb and al-Mustawrid, both saying: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity, for there will come a day when charity is not accepted."
"3261","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Jazui narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Marzuq informed us, Bakr ibn Bakkar narrated to us. And Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shuba, from Mabad ibn Khalid, from Haritha ibn Wahb: that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My Hawd is between Medina and Sanaa - so al-Mustawrid said to him: Did you not hear about the vessels? He said: The vessels; so al-Mustawrid said: In it are vessels like the stars. And the wording is that of the hadith of Zakariyya al-Saji."
"3262","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Salt ibn Bahram, from al-Harith ibn Wahb, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My nation remains upon a firm hold of its religion so long as they do not entrust funerals to their families."
"3263","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Waddah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Salt ibn Bahram, from al-Harith ibn Wahb, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My nation remains upon Islam so long as they do not delay Maghrib until the stars intertwine, in imitation of the Jews, and so long as they do not hasten Fajr, in imitation of the Christians, and so long as they do not entrust funerals to their families."
"3264","Those named al-Harith. 268 - Al-Harith ibn Nawfal ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim: Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, both saying: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught them the prayer over the dead: O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, mend our relations, and join our hearts. O Allah, this servant of Yours, so-and-so son of so-and-so, we know only good of him, and You know best of him, so forgive us and him. He said: So I said to him, while I was the youngest of the people: If I do not know good? He said: Then do not say but what you know."
"3265","Musa ibn Jumhur al-Simsar al-Tinnisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to us, Harun ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Anbasa, from Asim, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from his father, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the muadhdhin, he repeated what he said; and when he said: Come to prayer, come to success, he said: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"3266","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I came to a circle of the Banu Abd al-Muttalib, and I asked their elders: In how many garments was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shrouded? They said: In two red garments, with no shirt in them."
"3267","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muawiya, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I asked the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among them Ibn Nawfal: In what was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shrouded? They said: In a red hulla with no shirt in it, and there was placed in his grave a worn-out velvet cloth that belonged to them."
"3268","269 - Al-Harith ibn Ribi, Abu Qatada al-Ansari, then al-Sulami - and Abu Qatada was among the horsemen of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), may Allah be pleased with him: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr say: Abu Qatada is al-Harith ibn Ribi, and Abu Qatada was among the horsemen of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3269","Muhammad ibn al-Rabi ibn Shahin narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Ikrima ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salama ibn al-Akwa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of our horsemen today is Abu Qatada. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for him on the day of the ablution water."
"3270","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatada ibn Abd Allah ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatada, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, when he leaned from his mount, so I supported him with my hand until he awoke; then he leaned again, so I supported him with my hand until he awoke, and he said: O Allah, preserve Abu Qatada as he has preserved me since the night; I see we have only burdened you. And Abu Qatada used to dye with yellow."
"3271","Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Suraqa, who said: I saw Abu Qatada, Abu Hurayra, Ibn Umar, and Abu Usayd al-Saidi passing us while we were in the school; we found the scent of perfume from them, and they dyed their beards yellow."
"3272","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhram narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Yunus, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, who said: I saw Zayd ibn Thabit, Ibn Abbas, Abu Hurayra, and Abu Qatada wearing striped cloaks of silk."
"3273","Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Abu Qatada died - and his name is al-Harith ibn Ribi - in the year fifty-four, at the age of seventy."
"3274","Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Abu Qatada al-Harith ibn Ribi died in the year fifty-four."
"3275","And what Abu Qatada narrated: Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughba narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Abu Qatada: that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinate facing the qibla."
"3276","Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Dawud al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talha, I think from Anas ibn Malik, from Abu Qatada, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever wishes to be safe from the grief of the Day of Resurrection, let him grant respite to one in hardship or remit it from him."
"3277","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf and Shuayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Jafar, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Qatada, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sits upon the bed of an absent woman, a serpent is appointed for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"3278","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mabad or Abu Muhammad ibn Mabad narrated to us, from Abu Qatada: that al-Bara ibn Marur bequeathed a third of his wealth to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to dispose of as he wished, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it to his children."
"3279","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Rabia, from Abu al-Aswad, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Qatada, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit until he prays two rakats."
"3280","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Umar ibn Suhban, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Qatada, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that while he was on the pulpit addressing the people, a man came and sat down, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) extended his hand and said: O so-and-so, did you bow two rakats before sitting? He said: No. He said: What kept you? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I disliked craning my neck while you were standing. So he turned to us and said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him begin by bowing two rakats before sitting."
"3281","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abbad al-Abbadani narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu Sakhr, from Yahya ibn al-Nadr, from Abu Qatada, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the Hour, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What have you prepared for it? He said: Love of Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Then you are with whom you love."
"3282","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both saying: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Qatada, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst of people in theft is one who steals his prayer. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he steal his prayer? He said: He does not complete its bowing nor its prostration."
"3283","270 - Al-Harith ibn Awf, Abu Waqid al-Laythi - and it is said al-Harith ibn Malik, and it is said Awf ibn Malik, and it is said al-Harith ibn Awf: Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to me, saying: Abu Waqid al-Laythi died - and his name is al-Harith ibn Malik - in the year sixty-eight, at the age of seventy."
"3284","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini Fustuqa narrated to us, Harun al-Hammal narrated to us, saying: Abu Waqid al-Laythi died in the year sixty-eight, and the name of Abu Waqid is al-Harith ibn Malik, and it is said Awf ibn Malik."
"3285","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr say: Abu Waqid died in the year sixty-eight."
"3286","Muhammad ibn Sadaqa informed us, al-Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: I heard Yahya ibn Main say: Abu Waqid al-Laythi, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), is Awf ibn al-Harith."
"3287","Ubayd ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad al-Yazidi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sad narrated to us, al-Waqidi narrated to us, saying: Abu Waqid al-Laythi, his name is al-Harith ibn Malik. Muhammad ibn Sad said: And Hisham al-Kalbi said: al-Harith ibn Awf; and others besides them said: Awf ibn al-Harith ibn Usayd ibn Jabir ibn Ghurayra ibn Abd Manaf ibn Shuja ibn Amir ibn Layth."
"3288","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr say: Abu Waqid, and his name is al-Harith ibn Malik."
"3289","And what Abu Waqid al-Laythi narrated - Sinan ibn Abi Sinan from Abu Waqid: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sinan ibn Abi Sinan al-Duali, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) toward Hunayn, and we passed by a lote tree, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, make for us this Dhat Anw at as the disbelievers have a Dhat Anw at - and the disbelievers used to hang their weapons on a lote tree and stay around it - so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Greatest; this is as the Children of Israel said to Musa: Make for us a god as they have gods. You will surely ride the ways of those before you."
"3290","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Sinan ibn Abi Sinan al-Duali, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Hunayn while we were newly embracing disbelief, and the polytheists had a lote tree at which they stayed and upon which they hung their weapons, called Dhat Anw at. So we passed by the lote tree and said: O Messenger of Allah, make for us a Dhat Anw at as they have a Dhat Anw at. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Greatest; they are the ways. You have said, by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, as the Children of Israel said: Make for us a god as they have gods; you are an ignorant people. You will surely ride the ways of those before you."
"3291","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Sinan ibn Abi Sinan, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Hunayn, he passed by a tree called Dhat Anw at, upon which the polytheists hung their weapons, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, make for us a Dhat Anw at as they have a Dhat Anw at. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Greatest; this is as the Children of Israel said to Musa: Make for us a god as they have gods. You will surely ride the ways of those before you."
"3292","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Sinan ibn Abi Sinan al-Laythi, then al-Jundai, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were newly embracing Jahiliyya, and the disbelievers of Quraysh and other Arabs had a great tree called Dhat Anw at; they came to it every year, hung their weapons upon it, rested beneath it, and stayed by it for a day. As we traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we saw a great green lote tree, so we called out from the sides of the road: O Messenger of Allah, make for us a Dhat Anw at. He said: Allah is Greatest; you have said, by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, as the people of Musa said: Make for us a god as they have gods - the verse. You will surely ride the ways of those before you."
"3293","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sinan ibn Abi Sinan, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were newly embracing disbelief - and they had embraced Islam on the day of the Conquest - and we came to a tree upon which the polytheists hung their weapons and stayed by it yearly, called Dhat Anw at. So we said: Make for us a Dhat Anw at. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Greatest; you have said as the people of Musa said: Make for us a god as they have gods. Then he said: You will surely ride the ways of those before you."
"3294","Said ibn al-Musayyib from Abu Waqid: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Awwal narrated to us, Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Amin narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyib: that he heard Abu Waqid al-Laythi say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant among the servants of Allah was given the choice between the world, its kingdom and its bliss, and the Hereafter, and he chose the Hereafter. So Abu Bakr said: Rather we ransom you, O Messenger of Allah, with our wealth and ourselves."
"3295","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Awwal narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Amin narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyib: that he heard Abu Waqid say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The legs of my pulpit are fixed in Paradise."
"3296","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Himmani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Amin narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyib: that he heard Abu Waqid al-Laythi say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I been taking a close friend, I would have taken Ibn Abi Quhafa as a close friend; but your Companion is the close friend of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"3297","Urwa ibn al-Zubayr from Abu Waqid: Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, and Aisha: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led the people in prayer on the day of Fitr and Adha, and he said takbir seven times in the first rakat and recited: Qaf, by the Glorious Quran; and in the second five times, and recited: The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split."
"3298","Musa ibn Talha from Abu Waqid: Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both saying: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talha narrated to us, my uncle Musa ibn Talha narrated to me, Abu Waqid al-Laythi narrated to me, saying: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), my knee touching his knee, when a messenger came, took hold of his ear, and the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed, and blood rose to his forehead. Then he said: This is the messenger of Amir ibn al-Tufayl, threatening me and threatening those with me; Allah sufficed me against him through the sons of the offspring of Ismail, through the two sons of Qayla. Hisham said: Meaning the Ansar."
"3299","Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Waqid: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Hammam al-Dallal narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: We used to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when revelation came down to him, and he would narrate to us. One day he said to us: If the son of Adam had a valley, he would love to have a second to it; and if he had two valleys, he would love to have a third; and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust; then Allah turns to whoever repents."
"3300","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Waqid: that when revelation came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we came to him and he taught us what had been revealed to him. One day I came to him and he said: Allah the Exalted says: We sent down wealth for the establishment of prayer and the giving of zakat; and if the son of Adam had a valley, he would love to have a second to it; and if he had two, he would love to have a third to them; and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust; and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"3301","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, both saying: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhabbar narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when something came down to him he told us of it. One day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A verse came down to me: We sent down wealth for the establishment of prayer and the giving of zakat; and if the son of Adam had a valley he would seek a second to it; and if he had a second he would seek a third to it; and nothing fills the soul of the son of Adam but dust; and Allah turns to whoever repents. And Rabia ibn Uthman differed with Hisham ibn Sad and Ibn Mujabbar in the chain of this hadith."
"3302","Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Rabia ibn Uthman informed me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Mirawah, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic said: We sent down wealth for the establishment of prayer and the giving of zakat; and if the son of Adam had a valley he would love to have two valleys; and if he had two valleys he would love to have a third to them; and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust; and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"3303","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina while the people were cutting the humps of camels and cutting the tails of sheep, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever is cut from an animal while it is alive is carrion."
"3304","Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Abu Waqid: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Malik and Ibn Uyayna, from Damra ibn Said, who said: I heard Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba say: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, went out on a day of Eid and asked Abu Waqid al-Laythi: With what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in the Eid prayer? He said: With Qaf and Iqtarabat."
"3305","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Damra ibn Said, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, asked me what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited on the day of Eid, and I said: With Qaf, and: The Hour has drawn near."
"3306","Busr ibn Said from Abu Waqid: Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Ayyash ibn Abbas al-Utbani, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj: that Busr ibn Said narrated to him that Abu Waqid al-Laythi said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, while we were sitting on a mat: There will be tribulation. They said: What shall we do, O Messenger of Allah? So he returned his hand to the mat and grasped it, and said: Do like this. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned to them one day that there will be tribulation, but many people did not hear him, so Muadh ibn Jabal said: Do you not hear what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says? They said: What did he say? He said: There will be tribulation. They said: What shall we do, O Messenger of Allah, and how shall we act? He said: Return to your first affair."
"3307","Abu Murra, the freedman of Aqil ibn Abi Talib, from Abu Waqid: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talha: that Abu Murra, the freedman of Aqil, informed him from Abu Waqid al-Laythi: that while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the mosque with the people, three men came; two came toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and one went away. Two of them stood over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); one of them saw a gap in the circle and sat in it, the other sat behind them, and the third turned away. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: Shall I not tell you of the three men? As for one of them, he sought refuge with Allah, so Allah gave him refuge; as for the other, he was shy, so Allah was shy of him; and as for the other, he turned away, so Allah turned away from him."
"3308","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talha, from his freedman, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a circle, three men came; one man found a gap in the circle and sat in it, the other sat behind the circle, and another man went on. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not tell you of the three? As for the one who sat in the circle, he is a man who sought refuge, so Allah gave him refuge; as for the one who sat behind the circle, he is a man who was shy, so Allah was shy of him; and as for the one who turned away, Allah turned away from him."
"3309","Nafi ibn Sarjis from Abu Waqid: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym informed me, from Nafi ibn Sarjis, who said: We visited Abu Waqid al-Bakri in the illness in which he died, and I heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the lightest of people in prayer over the people, and the longest of people in prayer for himself."
"3310","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym informed me, Nafi ibn Sarjis narrated to me: that he entered upon Abu Waqid al-Laythi in the illness in which he died, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the lightest of people in prayer over the people, and the most constant in it for himself."
"3311","Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi al-Kufi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, Nafi ibn Sarjis narrated to me: that he entered upon Abu Waqid al-Laythi, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the lightest of people in prayer for the people, and the longest of people in prayer for himself."
"3312","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Nafi ibn Sarjis, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the lightest of people in prayer for the people, and the longest of people in prayer for himself."
"3313","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Nafi ibn Sarjis, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the lightest of people in prayer with the people, and the most constant in it for himself."
"3314","Abu Abd Allah Muslim ibn Mishkam from Abu Waqid: Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim informed us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Atiyya, from Marthad or Abu Marthad, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi: that they said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land where hunger strikes us; what of carrion is lawful for us? He said: When you have not drunk evening milk, nor morning milk, nor gathered vegetables, then partake of it."
"3315","Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi and Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, both saying: al-Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Subh al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Kathir al-Qurashi narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Hassan ibn Atiyya narrated to us, Muslim narrated to me, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land where hunger strikes us; what of carrion is fit for us? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you have not drunk morning milk, nor evening milk, nor gathered vegetables, then partake of it."
"3316","Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Waqid from his father: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Zubala al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Harun ibn Yahya ibn Harun ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Waqid al-Laythi narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Waqid: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes repeatedly to this prayer, his past sins are forgiven."
"3317","Waqid ibn Abi Waqid from his father: Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamza al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Waqid ibn Abi Waqid, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his wives in the Farewell Hajj: This, then the backs of mats (i.e. stay at home)."
"3318","271 - Al-Harith ibn Adi ibn Malik al-Ansari, martyred on the Day of the Bridge in the year fifteen: al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those martyred on the Day of the Bridge in the year fifteen among the Ansar, then among Banu Muawiya: al-Harith ibn Adi ibn Malik."
"3319","272 - Al-Harith ibn Masud ibn Abd ibn Muzahir: al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those martyred on the Day of the Bridge in the year fifteen: al-Harith ibn Masud ibn Abd ibn Muzahir."
"3320","Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, concerning the naming of those martyred on the Day of the Bridge among the Ansar, then among Banu Muawiya: al-Harith ibn Masud ibn Abd ibn Muzahir."
"3321","273 - Al-Harith ibn Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari, a Badri: al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Ansari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those present at Badr among the Ansar, then among Banu al-Nabit, then among Banu Abd al-Ashhal: al-Harith ibn Anas ibn Malik ibn Ubayd ibn Kab."
"3322","274 - Al-Harith ibn Aws al-Ansari, a Badri: al-Hasan ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those present at Badr among the Ansar, among Banu al-Nabit, then among Banu Abd al-Ashhal: al-Harith ibn Aws."
"3323","275 - Al-Harith ibn Hassan al-Bakri: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Anbasa ibn al-Azhar, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: Al-Harith ibn Hassan married - and he had companionship - and at that time when a man married he would stay secluded for days and not go out for the dawn prayer. It was said to him: Do you go out when you have just consummated with your wife last night? He said: By Allah, a wife who keeps me from the dawn prayer in congregation is an evil wife."
"3324","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim and Muhammad ibn Makhlad al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir al-Qari informed us, Asim ibn Bahdala narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from al-Harith ibn Hassan, who said: I passed by an old woman at al-Rabadha, stranded among Banu Tamim, and she said: Where are you heading? We said: We head to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Carry me with you, for I have a need with him. I entered the mosque, and the mosque was crowded with people, and a black banner was fluttering, with Bilal girt with a sword standing before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I sat in the mosque, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, he gave me permission and I entered. He said: Was there anything between you and Tamim? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah; victory was ours over them. I passed by an old woman of theirs at al-Rabadha, stranded, and she said: I have a need with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I carried her, and there she is at the door. He permitted her and she entered. When she sat, I said: O Messenger of Allah, if you see fit to make al-Dahna between us and Tamim, do so, for it was once ours. The old woman sprang up, seized by zeal, and said: O Messenger of Allah, where do you force your Mudar? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am, by Allah, as the first one said: Bakr carried its own death; I carried this woman without knowing she would be an adversary to me. I seek refuge in Allah and His Messenger from being like the envoy of Ad. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And who is the envoy of Ad? I said: You have met an expert. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He keeps asking me for the story. And Affan said: I seek refuge in Allah from being as the first one said. He said: And what did the first one say? He said: You have met an expert. He said: Come on, he keeps asking him for the story. He said: Ad suffered drought, so they sent their envoy Qayl, who stayed with Muawiya ibn Bakr for a month, plying him with wine while the two singing girls sang to him - Sallam said: meaning the two slave singers. Then he went on to the mountains of Mahra and said: O Allah, You know I did not come to ransom a captive nor to treat a sick man, so give Your servant to drink what You will give him, and give with him Muawiya ibn Bakr a month, in gratitude for the wine he drank with him. Then black clouds passed, and he was called from them: Choose the cloud. He said: This is a black cloud. He was called from it: Take it as ashes, most ashen, leaving none of Ad. I said: O Messenger of Allah, it reached me that there was not sent upon them of the wind but as much as is seen in a ring. Abu Wail said: And likewise it reached us."
"3325","Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Sallam Abu al-Mundhir, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from al-Harith ibn Hassan, who said: I came to Medina and saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering a sermon, with Bilal girt with a sword and black banners planted; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sent Amr ibn al-As."
"3326","Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both saying: Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Thalabi and al-Ala ibn Amr al-Hanafi narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Harith ibn Hassan, who said: I came to Medina and saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing on the pulpit, with Bilal standing before him girt with a sword, and black banners. I said: What are these? They said: Amr ibn al-As has come from a raid."
"3327","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Asim ibn Abi al-Najud narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Hassan al-Bakri, who said: We came to Medina, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the pulpit, with Bilal standing before him girt with a sword before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and black banners. I said: What are these banners? They said: Amr ibn al-As has come from a raid."
"3328","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me. And Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Asim ibn Abi al-Najud narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Hassan al-Bakri, who said: We came to Medina, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the pulpit, with Bilal standing before him girt with a sword before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and black banners. I asked: What are these banners? He said: Amr ibn al-As has come from a raid."
"3329","276 - Al-Harith ibn Malik ibn Barsa al-Laythi - and he is al-Harith ibn Malik ibn Qays ibn Uwaydh ibn Abd Allah ibn Jabir ibn Abd Manat ibn Shuja ibn Amir ibn Layth ibn Bakr ibn Abd Manat ibn Kinana: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Umar ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Riyahi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayya, from Umar ibn Ata ibn Abi Khuwar, from Ubayd ibn Jurayj, from al-Harith ibn al-Barsa, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while walking between the two Jamras, say: Whoever takes anything of a Muslims wealth by a wicked oath, let him take a house in the Fire."
"3330","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ismail ibn Umayya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi al-Khuwar, a freedman of Banu Amir, who said: I heard al-Harith ibn al-Barsa, during the season, calling out among the people - Sufyan said: I know only that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none who swears a false oath to cut off thereby the right of a Muslim, but he meets Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, while He is angry with him."
"3331","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Ismail ibn Umayya, from Umar ibn Ata ibn Abi al-Khuwar, from al-Harith ibn Malik ibn Barsa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"3332","Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, from al-Shabi, who said: I heard al-Harith ibn Malik ibn al-Barsa say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on the day of the Conquest of Mecca: It (Mecca) shall not be raided after this until the Day of Resurrection."
"3333","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Amir al-Shabi, from al-Harith ibn Malik ibn al-Barsa, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest of Mecca say: It shall not be raided after this until the Day of Resurrection."
"3334","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir and Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Zakariyya, from al-Shabi, from al-Harith ibn Malik ibn Barsa, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on the day of the Conquest of Mecca: It shall not be raided after this day until the Day of Resurrection."
"3335","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from al-Harith ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"3336","3337 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, and Asbat ibn Muhammad, from Zakariya, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"3337","3338 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Zakariya narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah saying: It shall never be raided after this day ever. Sufyan said: Its explanation is: upon disbelief."
"3338","277 - Al-Harith ibn Hisham al-Makhzumi: he was martyred on the day of Yarmuk in the year fifteen, and he is al-Harith ibn Hisham ibn al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Makhzum, his kunyah Abu Abd al-Rahman, and his mother Asma bint Makhramah ibn Jandal ibn Amir ibn Nahshal ibn Darim ibn Malik ibn Hanzalah ibn Malik ibn Zayd Manat ibn Tamim; he accepted Islam on the day of the conquest, and he was among those whose hearts were to be reconciled, and he died in the year eighteen in Sham. 3339 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, who said: Al-Harith ibn Hisham died in Sham in the year eighteen."
"3339","3340 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Madini Fustuqah narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn Uthman and countless others informed me, from Ibn Haramah; al-Zubayr said: And Nawfal ibn Maymun narrated to me, Abu Malik Muhammad ibn Malik ibn Ali ibn Haramah recited to me, for his uncle Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Haramah:"
"3340","3341 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Baghdadi al-Madini narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, who said: Ibn al-Kawsaj, the freedman of the family of Abu Farwah, said to a man:"
"3341","3342 - Musa ibn Zakariya al-Tustari narrated to us, Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, Abu Wahb al-Sahmi narrated to us, from Abu Yunus al-Qushayri, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, that al-Harith ibn Hisham, Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl, and Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah were fatally wounded on the day of Yarmuk, so al-Harith called for a drink, Ikrimah looked at him and said: Pass it to Ikrimah, so it was passed to him, then Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah looked at it, so Ikrimah said: Pass it to Ayyash, and it did not reach any of them before they all died without tasting it."
"3342","3343 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Amir ibn Salih narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, from al-Harith ibn Hisham that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How does the revelation come down to you? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Like the ringing of a bell, then it leaves me after I have retained what he said. He said: And it is the hardest upon me, and sometimes the angel comes to me and appears to me and speaks to me what he says."
"3343","3344 - Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Aruzzi narrated to us, Asim ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Harith ibn Hisham, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How does the revelation come to you? He said: It comes to me as a ringing like the ringing of a bell, and sometimes it comes to me in the form of a man who speaks to me, and that is easier upon me, then it leaves me after I have retained it."
"3344","3345 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Malik narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah that al-Harith ibn Hisham asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How does the revelation come to you? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell, and it is the hardest upon me, then it leaves me after I have retained what he said, and sometimes the angel appears to me as a man and speaks to me and I retain what he says. Aishah said: And I saw him with revelation descending upon him on an intensely cold day, then it would leave him while his forehead dripped with sweat."
"3345","3346 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Yazid al-Tahhan narrated to us, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: Al-Harith ibn Hisham asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) how the revelation comes to him. He said: Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell, then it leaves me after I have retained it, and it is the hardest upon me, and sometimes the angel comes to me in the form of a man and I retain what he says."
"3346","3347 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Abd al-Malik ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Umm Salamah in Shawwal and brought her to himself in Shawwal."
"3347","3348 - Zakariya al-Saji narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibn Sam'an informed me that Ibn Shihab informed him that Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'id al-Muq'ad informed him that Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed him that his father al-Harith ibn Hisham informed him that he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Inform me of a matter to hold fast to. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Control this, and he pointed to his tongue."
"3348","3349 - Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both saying: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from his father that he said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a matter to hold fast to. He said: Keep this over you, and he pointed to his tongue."
"3349","278 - Al-Harith ibn Amr al-Sahmi. 3350 - Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, (h). And al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, (h). And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Abu Salamah Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Zurarah ibn Karaym ibn al-Harith ibn Amr narrated to us, who said: My father narrated to me, from his grandfather al-Harith ibn Amr, that he met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage while he was upon his she-camel al-Adba. He said: I said: May my father and mother be ransomed for you, O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me, so he said: May Allah forgive you. Then I turned around from the other side hoping he would single me out, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me, so he said: May Allah forgive you. Then a man said: O Messenger of Allah, the fara' and the ata'ir? He said: Whoever wishes may offer the fara' and whoever wishes may not, and whoever wishes may offer the atirah and whoever wishes may not, and for sheep is its sacrifice. Then he said: Verily your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours in this month of yours."
"3350","3351 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ma'mar al-Muq'ad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Utbah ibn Abd al-Malik al-Sahmi narrated to us, Zurarah ibn Karaym ibn al-Harith ibn Amr al-Sahmi narrated to me, that al-Harith ibn Amr narrated to him, saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at Mina or at Arafat, and the Bedouins would come, and when they saw his face they said: This is a blessed face. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me. He said: O Allah, forgive us. He said: So I went around and said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me. He said: O Allah, forgive us. Then he was about to spit, so he gestured with his hand and took his spittle in it and wiped his sandal with it, disliking that it should touch anyone around him. Then he said: O people, what day is this? For your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours in this month of yours in this land of yours. O Allah, have I conveyed? And let the witness convey to the absent. He said: And he commanded charity and said: Give charity, for I do not know, perhaps you will not see me after this day of mine. And he appointed Yalamlam for the people of Yemen to enter ihram from it, and Dhat Irq for the people of Iraq, or he said: for the people of the east. And a man asked him about the atirah. He said: Whoever wishes may offer the atirah and whoever wishes may not, and whoever wishes may offer the fara' and whoever wishes may not. And he said: For sheep is its sacrifice, with the fingers of his right palm, pouring them upon the joint of the middle finger and his index finger, bending its tip somewhat."
"3351","3352 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sahl ibn Husayn al-Bahili narrated to me, Zurarah ibn Kuraym narrated to me, from al-Harith ibn Amr al-Sahmi, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage while he was upon his she-camel al-Adba, and al-Harith was a bulky man, so al-Harith dismounted to him and drew near him until his face was level with the knee of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached out wiping the face of al-Harith, and a radiance remained upon the face of al-Harith until he died. So al-Harith said to him: O Prophet of Allah, supplicate to Allah for me. So he said: O Allah, forgive us. Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Abd al-Warith."
"3352","279 - Al-Harith ibn Abd Allah ibn Aws al-Thaqafi. 3353 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, (h). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Harith ibn Abd Allah ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, who said: I asked Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, about a woman who circumambulates the House then menstruates. He said: Let her last covenant be the circumambulation of the House. So al-Harith said: Thus did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rule for me. So Umar said: You have rubbed dirt upon your hand; you asked me about a thing you had asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about, so that I would differ."
"3353","3354 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, (h). And Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, both from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah al-Ta'ifi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani, from Amr ibn Aws, from al-Harith ibn Abd Allah al-Thaqafi, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever performs hajj or umrah, let his last covenant be that he circumambulate the House. So Umar said: Scratch from your hand; you heard this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and did not inform me."
"3354","3355 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah al-Ta'ifi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani, from Amr ibn Aws, from al-Harith ibn Abd Allah ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"3355","280 - Al-Harith ibn Ziyad al-Ansari, then al-Sa'idi, a Badri. 3356 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both saying: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman ibn al-Ghasil narrated to us, Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd narrated to me - and his father was a Badri - al-Harith ibn Ziyad al-Sa'idi informed me that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Trench while he was pledging the people upon emigration, so we thought they were being called to the pledge, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, pledge this one. He said: Who is this? He said: This is my cousin Hawt ibn Yazid, or Yazid ibn Hawt. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not pledge you; the people emigrate to you and you do not emigrate to them. Then he said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no man loves the Ansar until he meets Allah but he meets Allah while He loves him, and no man hates the Ansar until he meets Allah but he meets Allah while He hates him."
"3356","3357 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Mundhir, from Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd al-Ansari, from al-Harith ibn Ziyad, and he was among the companions of Badr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him until he meets Him, and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah hates him until he meets Him."
"3357","3358 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Mundhir, from Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd, from al-Harith ibn Ziyad, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him when he meets Him, and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah hates him when he meets Him."
"3358","281 - Al-Harith ibn Uqaysh al-Ukli. 3359 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, (h). And Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abd Allah ibn Qays, who said: I heard al-Harith ibn Uqaysh narrating to Abu Burdah, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There are no two Muslims who lose four and bear them patiently, hoping for reward, but they enter Paradise. So it was said: O Messenger of Allah, and three? He said: And three. It was said: And two? He said: And two."
"3359","3360 - Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, al-Mu'alla ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abd Allah ibn Qays, from al-Harith ibn Uqaysh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who loses four of his children but Allah admits him to Paradise by virtue of His mercy to them. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and three? He said: And three. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and two? He said: And two. He said: And among my ummah there is one who grows until he becomes one of its corners, and among my ummah there is one through whose intercession enter more than Mudar."
"3360","3361 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abd Allah ibn Qays, from al-Harith ibn Uqaysh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of my ummah shall enter Paradise and intercede for more than Mudar, and a man of my ummah shall grow for the Fire until he becomes one of its corners, and there are no two Muslims who send forth four of their children but Allah admits them to Paradise by virtue of His mercy. So they said: Or three? He said: Or three. They said: Or two? He said: Or two."
"3361","3362 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Abu Ma'mar al-Muq'ad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abd Allah ibn Qays, from al-Harith ibn Uqaysh, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no Muslim man and woman who lose four of their children who have not reached puberty but Allah admits them to Paradise. Then he mentioned the like of it."
"3362","3363 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, Abd Allah ibn Qays narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Uqaysh, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among my ummah is one who enters Paradise, through his intercession more than Mudar."
"3363","3364 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Qatan ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Qays, from al-Harith ibn Uqaysh, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it, except that he said: So Abd Allah said to him."
"3364","3365 - Al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abd Allah ibn Qays, from al-Harith ibn Uqaysh, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"3365","3366 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Awwal narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abd Allah ibn Qays, from al-Harith ibn Uqaysh, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"3366","282 - Al-Harith ibn Malik al-Ansari. 3367 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid al-Saksaki, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Jahm, from al-Harith ibn Malik al-Ansari, that he passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said to him: How have you woken, O Harith? He said: I have woken a true believer. So he said: Look at what you say, for everything has a reality, so what is the reality of your faith? So he said: My soul has turned away from the world, and I have kept my night awake for that, and made my day thirsty, and it is as though I look at the Throne of my Lord manifest, and as though I look at the people of Paradise visiting one another therein, and as though I look at the people of the Fire wailing therein. So he said: O Harith, you have known, so hold fast, three times."
"3367","283 - Al-Harith ibn Badal al-Tamimi. 3368 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, my uncle Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, (h). And Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinna'i and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shu'aythi narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Badal, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn, and all his companions fled except al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw our faces with a handful of earth and we were routed, and it seemed to me that no tree nor stone but was in our tracks."
"3368","284 - Al-Harith ibn Sawwad al-Ansari, a Badri. 3369 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr: al-Harith ibn Sawwad."
"3369","285 - Al-Harith, and it is said Harithah ibn Suraqah al-Ansari, a Badri, he was martyred on the day of Badr. 3370 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those martyred on the day of Badr among the Ansar, then among Banu al-Najjar, then among Banu Adi ibn al-Najjar: al-Harith ibn Suraqah ibn al-Harith."
"3370","3371 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, in naming those martyred on the day of Badr among the Ansar, then among Banu al-Najjar: Harithah ibn Suraqah."
"3371","286 - Al-Harith ibn al-Harith al-Ghamidi. 3372 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Rafi' narrated to us, Umar ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Adi ibn Hilal al-Sulami, from al-Harith ibn al-Harith, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying upon finishing his food: O Allah, to You is praise; You fed and gave drink and satisfied and quenched; to You is praise, not denied nor bidden farewell nor dispensed with, our Lord."
"3372","3373 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both saying: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Ismail ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jurashi narrated to us, al-Harith ibn al-Harith al-Ghamidi narrated to us, who said: I said to my father: What is this crowd? He said: These people have gathered upon a Sabian of theirs. He said: So we dismounted, and behold the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calling the people to the oneness of Allah, mighty and majestic, and faith in Him, while they rebuffed him and hurt him, until midday came and the people dispersed from him, and a woman came with her neck exposed carrying a cup and a napkin, so he took it from her and drank and performed ablution, then raised his head and said: O my daughter, cover your neck, and do not fear for your father. We said: Who is this? They said: Zaynab, his daughter."
"3373","287 - Al-Harith ibn al-Harith ibn Qays al-Qurashi, then al-Sahmi, he was killed on the day of Ajnadayn. 3374 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those killed on the day of Ajnadayn among the Muslims, then among Quraysh, then among Banu Sahm: al-Harith ibn al-Harith ibn Qays."
"3374","3375 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, in naming those martyred on the day of Ajnadayn among Quraysh, then among Banu Sahm: al-Harith ibn Abi Qarib."
"3375","3376 - Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, in naming those martyred on the day of Ajnadayn among Quraysh, then among Banu Sahm: al-Harith ibn al-Harith."
"3376","288 - Al-Harith ibn Qays ibn Makhlad al-Ansari, then al-Zuraqi, an Aqabi Badri, his kunyah Abu Khalid. 3377 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming the companions of al-Aqabah among the Ansar, then among Banu Zurayq: al-Harith ibn Qays ibn Makhlad, and he witnessed Badr, and he is Abu Khalid."
"3377","3378 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed al-Aqabah among the Ansar, then among Banu Zurayq: al-Harith ibn Qays ibn Khalid ibn Makhlad; he witnessed Badr."
"3378","289 - Al-Harith ibn Mu'adh ibn al-Nu'man, the brother of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh al-Ansari, a Badri. 3379 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then among al-Aws, then among Banu Abd al-Ashhal: al-Harith ibn Mu'adh ibn al-Nu'man."
"3379","290 - Al-Harith ibn al-Simmah al-Ansari, a Badri; he was killed on the day of Bi'r Ma'unah. 3380 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then among Banu Amir ibn Malik ibn al-Najjar, then among Banu Amir ibn Mabdhul: al-Harith ibn al-Simmah ibn Ubayd ibn Amir."
"3380","3381 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, in naming those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, among Banu Amir ibn Malik: al-Harith ibn al-Simmah ibn Amr ibn Ubayd ibn Amr ibn Mabdhul; he was broken at al-Rawha, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck for him with his arrow."
"3381","3382 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then among Banu Amir ibn Malik ibn al-Najjar, then among Banu Mabdhul: al-Harith ibn al-Simmah ibn Amr ibn Atik; he was broken at al-Rawha, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck for him with his arrow."
"3382","3383 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those killed among the Muslims on the day of Bi'r Ma'unah: al-Harith ibn al-Simmah."
"3383","3384 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, in naming those martyred among the Muslims on the day of Bi'r Ma'unah: al-Harith ibn al-Simmah."
"3384","3385 - Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbadah al-Wasiti narrated to us, (h). And Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, both saying: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Dinar, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, who said: Al-Harith ibn al-Simmah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked me on the day of Uhud while he was in the mountain pass: Have you seen Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I saw him toward the hot part of the mountain, with a throng of polytheists upon him, so I ran to him to defend him, then I saw you and turned to you. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily the angels fight alongside him. Al-Harith said: So I returned to Abd al-Rahman and found him among seven fallen men, so I said to him: Your right hand has triumphed; did you kill all of these? He said: As for this one, of Artah ibn Shurahbil, and this one, I killed them both, and as for these, they were killed by one I did not see. I said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth."
"3385","291 - Al-Harith ibn Aws ibn al-Nu'man al-Ansari. 3386 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, that Sa'd ibn Mu'adh sent al-Harith ibn Aws ibn al-Nu'man, the brother of Banu Harithah, with Muhammad ibn Maslamah to Ibn al-Ashraf, and when he struck Ibn al-Ashraf, the edge of the sword hit the leg of al-Harith, so his companions carried him."
"3386","292 - Al-Harith ibn Aws ibn Rafi' al-Ansari; he was martyred on the day of Uhud. 3387 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those martyred on the day of Uhud among the Ansar, then among Banu Amr ibn Awf: al-Harith ibn Aws ibn Rafi'."
"3387","3388 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, in naming those martyred on the day of Uhud among the Ansar, among Banu al-Nabit: al-Harith ibn Aws ibn Rafi'."
"3388","293 - Al-Harith ibn Ashyam ibn Rafi' ibn Imri' al-Qays al-Ansari, then al-Ashhali, a Badri. 3389 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then among al-Aws, then among Banu Abd al-Ashhal: al-Harith ibn Ashyam ibn Rafi' ibn Imri' al-Qays ibn Zayd ibn Abd al-Ashhal."
"3389","294 - Al-Harith ibn Ghaziyah. 3390 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, (h). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, both from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwah, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi' narrated to me, from al-Harith ibn Ghaziyah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah saying: There is no emigration after the conquest; it is only faith and intention."
"3390","3391 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah, that Abd Allah ibn Rafi' informed him, from al-Harith ibn Ghaziyah, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah saying: Temporary marriage with women is forbidden, three times."
"3391","295 - Al-Harith ibn al-Nu'man al-Ansari, a Badri. 3392 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then among Banu Tha'labah ibn Amr ibn Awf: al-Harith ibn al-Nu'man."
"3392","3393 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then among Banu al-Aws, then among Banu Tha'labah ibn Amr ibn Awf: al-Harith ibn al-Nu'man."
"3393","3394 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, in naming those who witnessed with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: al-Harith ibn al-Nu'man, a Badri."
"3394","296 - Al-Harith ibn Sirar al-Khuza'i. 3395 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Attab Abu Bakr al-A'yan narrated to me, (h). And Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani narrated to us, (h). And Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Hammal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Zajjaj narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Sabiq informed us, Isa ibn Dinar al-Mu'min narrated to us, my father narrated to me that he heard al-Harith ibn Sirar al-Khuza'i saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he invited me to Islam, so I entered it and affirmed it, and he invited me to zakat, so I affirmed it. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shall return to my people and invite them to Islam and payment of zakat, and whoever responds to me among them, I shall collect his zakat, so send, O Messenger of Allah, a messenger at such-and-such a time who will bring you what I have collected of zakat. When al-Harith had collected the zakat from those who responded to him and the time arrived which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wished to send to him, the messenger was held back from him and did not come to him, so al-Harith thought that displeasure from Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had occurred against him, so he called the chiefs of his people and said to them: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had appointed for me a time to send his messenger to me to take what was with me of zakat, and breaking a promise is not of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I see the withholding of his messenger only as due to displeasure that occurred, so come, let us go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sent al-Walid ibn Uqbah to al-Harith to take what was with him of what he had collected of zakat, and when al-Walid had traveled until he reached part of the way, he became frightened and returned, and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, al-Harith withheld the zakat from me and intended to kill me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dispatched an expedition to al-Harith, and al-Harith came forward with his companions, until when the expedition faced him, having set out from Madinah, al-Harith met them. They said: This is al-Harith. When he reached them he said to them: To whom have you been sent? They said: To you. He said: And why? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sent al-Walid ibn Uqbah, and he returned claiming that you withheld the zakat and intended to kill him. So he said: No, by the One Who sent Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the truth, I neither saw him nor did he come to me, and I came forward only when a messenger was withheld from me, fearing it be displeasure from Allah and His Messenger, peace be upon him. Then al-Hujurat was revealed: O you who believe, if a transgressor comes to you with news, verify, lest you harm a people in ignorance and become regretful over what you did, up to this place: A bounty from Allah and a blessing, and Allah is Knowing, Wise."
"3395","297 - Al-Harith ibn al-Nu'man al-Ansari; he was killed on the day of Mu'tah. 3396 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those killed on the day of Mu'tah among the Ansar: al-Harith ibn al-Nu'man ibn Yasaf ibn Nadlah ibn Abd Awf ibn Ghanm."
"3396","298 - Al-Harith ibn Khazmah ibn Abi Ghanm al-Ansari, a Badri. 3397 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar: al-Harith ibn Khazmah ibn Abi Ghanm ibn Salim ibn Awf ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj."
"3397","3398 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then among Banu al-Nabit, then among Banu Abd al-Ashhal: al-Harith ibn Khazmah ibn Adi, an ally of theirs from Banu Salim."
"3398","299 - Al-Harith ibn Ghutayf al-Kindi. 3399 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Yunus ibn Sayf, (h). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both saying: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Yunus ibn Sayf al-Ansi, from al-Harith ibn Ghutayf, or Ghutayf ibn al-Harith al-Kindi, who said: Whatever I forget, I have not forgotten that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to place his right hand upon his left in prayer. Abu Rashid was not mentioned."
"3399","3400 - Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Yunus ibn Sayf, from Abu Rashid al-Hubrani, from al-Harith ibn Ghutayf, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his right upon his left in prayer."
"3400","300 - Al-Harith ibn Hatib al-Ansari, a Badri. 3401 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then among al-Aws, then among Banu Amr ibn Awf, then among Banu Umayyah ibn Zayd: al-Harith ibn Hatib."
"3401","3402 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, in naming those who witnessed with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: al-Harith ibn Hatib al-Ansari, of Banu Harithah; he returned from al-Rawha."
"3402","3403 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck for a number of the Emigrants and the Ansar with their full shares on the day of Badr, though they were absent from it due to an excuse they had; among them of the Ansar were Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir and al-Harith ibn Hatib."
"3403","301 - Al-Harith ibn Amr, the uncle of al-Bara ibn Azib, a Badri. 3404 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ash'ath, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Yazid ibn al-Bara, from his father, who said: I met my uncle with a banner with him, so I said: Where are you heading? So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a man who married his father's wife, and commanded me to kill him."
"3404","3405 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, (h). And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to me, Hushaym narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn Sawwar informed us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Yazid ibn al-Bara, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: Al-Harith ibn Amr passed by me, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had tied a banner for him, so I said: To where has the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent you? So he said: He sent me to a man who married his father's wife after him, to strike his neck."
"3405","3406 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Waki'i al-Misri narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Yazid ibn al-Bara, from his father, who said: I met my uncle having fastened a banner, so I said: Where are you heading? So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a man who married his father's wife, to strike his neck and take his wealth. Thus did Ash'ath ibn Sawwar and Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah report it, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Yazid ibn al-Bara, from his father, who said: I met my uncle. And al-Suddi differed from them, reporting it from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara, who said: I met my maternal uncle. And his maternal uncle is Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, and he did not place Yazid between Adi and al-Bara."
"3406","3407 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: I met my maternal uncle with a banner with him, so I said: Where are you going? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a man who married his father's wife after him, to strike his neck and kill him."
"3407","302 - Al-Harith ibn Hatib al-Jumahi, and he is al-Harith ibn Hatib ibn al-Harith ibn Ma'mar ibn Habib ibn Wahb ibn Hudhafah ibn Jumah, and his mother Fatimah bint al-Mujallil ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Qays ibn Abd Wudd ibn Nadr ibn Malik ibn Hasal; she emigrated with him to the land of Abyssinia with her husband Hatib ibn al-Harith. 3408 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih al-Ijli narrated to us, (h). And Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, (h). And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i al-Qadi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, (h). And Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Sa'd, from al-Harith ibn Hatib, that a thief was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Kill him. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, he only stole. He said: Kill him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, he only stole. He said: Cut off his hand. Then he stole and his leg was cut off, then he stole in the time of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, until all his limbs were cut off, then he stole a fifth time, so Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew better about him when he said: Kill him."
"3408","3409 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Yusuf ibn Ya'qub, from Muhammad ibn Hatib, that al-Harith ibn Hatib mentioned Ibn al-Zubayr and said: How long he coveted leadership. We said: And what is that? He said: A thief was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he ordered his killing, so it was said to him: He stole, so he said: Cut him. Then he was brought after that to Abu Bakr, having stolen, with his limbs cut off, so Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I find nothing for you but what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed concerning you on the day he ordered your killing, for he knew better about you. Then he ordered his killing, young boys among the sons of the Emigrants, I among them, so Ibn al-Zubayr said: Appoint me over us, then we took him. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"3409","303 - Al-Harith Abu Malik al-Ash'ari. Rabi'ah al-Jurashi from Abu Malik. 3410 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Qatadah ibn al-Fudayl al-Ruhawi narrated to us, who said: I heard Hisham ibn al-Ghaz narrating from his father, from his grandfather, that Abu Malik said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There shall be in my ummah collapse, transformation, and pelting. We said: In what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: By their taking singing girls, and their drinking of wines."
"3410","Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari. 3411 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, that Abu Malik al-Ash'ari said to his people: Gather, I shall pray with you the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he had gathered them, he said: Is there among you any of other than you? They said: No, except a nephew of ours. He said: The nephew of a people is of them. Then he called for a basin with water in it, so he washed his hands and rinsed and sniffed, and washed his face three times, and his forearms three times, and wiped his head, and washed his feet, then prayed with them Zuhr, and uttered in it twenty-two takbirs, uttering takbir when he prostrated and when he raised his head from prostration, and recited in the first two rak'ahs the Opening of the Book, letting those next to him hear."
"3411","3412 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that he gathered his companions and said: Shall I pray with you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? And he was a man of the Ash'aris. Then he called for a basin of water, so he washed his hands three times, and rinsed and sniffed three times, and washed his face three times and his forearms, and wiped his head and his ears, and wiped his feet, and prayed Zuhr, and prayed in it with the Opening of the Book, and uttered twenty-two takbirs."
"3412","3413 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that he said to his people: Gather, I shall pray with you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they gathered, and he said: Is there among you any? So they said: No, except a nephew of ours. He said: Then that is of the people. Then he called for a basin with water in it, so he performed ablution with them witnessing, and rinsed and sniffed three times, and washed his face three times and his forearms three times, and wiped his head and the tops of his feet, then prayed with them Zuhr, and uttered in it twenty-two takbirs, uttering takbir when he prostrated and when he raised his head, and recited with them in the first two rak'ahs, letting those next to him hear."
"3413","3414 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Isa al-Ta'i narrated to us, Talhah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that he said: Gather, I shall pray with you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they gathered, and he said: Is among you any of other than you? They said: No, except a nephew of ours. He said: The nephew of a people is of them. Then he called for a basin and performed ablution from it, and rinsed and sniffed, and washed his face three times, and his hands three times, and wiped his head and the tops of his feet, and stepped forward and prayed with them Zuhr, and recited the Opening of the Book letting those next to him hear."
"3414","3415 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that he said: Come, that I show you how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray? So he stood and uttered takbir when he bowed and when he prostrated, and when he rose from sitting after the two rak'ahs he uttered takbir."
"3415","3416 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ayyash ibn al-Walid al-Raqqam narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Budayl ibn Maysarah narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, who said: Abu Malik al-Ash'ari said: I shall surely pray with you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he called for ablution water and performed ablution, then stood for prayer, and arranged the men and arranged the boys behind them, and kept uttering takbir when he prostrated and when he raised his head and when he rose from the two rak'ahs, then greeted to his right and to his left. And Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm was not mentioned."
"3416","3417 - Musa ibn Sahl al-Jawni al-Basri narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ibn Jabir narrated to us, Atiyyah ibn Qays al-Kilabi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm narrated to us, Abu Amir or Abu Malik al-Ash'ari narrated to me - by Allah, he did not lie to me - that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There shall be in my ummah peoples who deem silk, wine, and musical instruments lawful, and peoples shall settle beside a mountain with their grazing livestock coming to them, then a man comes to them for his need, so they say to him: Return to us tomorrow, so Allah, mighty and majestic, destroys them by night and lays the mountain upon them, and transforms others into apes and pigs until the Day of Resurrection."
"3417","3418 - Khayr ibn Arafah al-Misri narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Himsi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibn Thawban, from his father, referring it to Makhul, to Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm al-Ash'ari, that Abu Malik al-Ash'ari said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: Whoever goes out volunteering in My path as a warrior, seeking My face, affirming My promise, and believing in My messengers, he is guaranteed by Allah, mighty and majestic: either He takes him in the army by whatever death He wills and admits him to Paradise, or he roams under the guarantee of Allah, mighty and majestic, even if his absence is long, until He returns him to his family with what he attained of reward and booty. And he said: Whoever sets out in the path of Allah and dies or is killed, or his horse or camel throws him, or a venomous creature stings him, or he dies upon his bed by whatever death Allah wills, he is a martyr."
"3418","3419 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Hatim ibn Hurayth, from Malik ibn Abi Maryam al-Hakami, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm al-Ash'ari came to Damascus, and a group of us gathered to him, and we mentioned tila, some of us permitting it and some of us disliking it, so I came to him after we had delved into it, and he said: I heard Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, the companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Peoples of my ummah shall surely drink wine calling it by other than its name, and musical instruments and singing girls shall be played over their heads; Allah shall cause the earth to swallow them, and make of them apes and pigs."
"3419","3420 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from Utbah ibn Humayd, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Ibn Ghanm, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the completion of righteousness? He said: That you do in secret the deed of openness."
"3420","3421 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariya al-Iyadi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us, and when he finished his prayer he turned to the people with his face."
"3421","3422 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Miskin al-Yamami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and when he bowed he said: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, three times, then raised his head."
"3422","Abu Sallam al-Aswad from al-Harith al-Ash'ari. 3423 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, (h). And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, both saying: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me that Zayd ibn Sallam narrated to him, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Purity is half of faith, and praise be to Allah fills the scale, and glory be to Allah and Allah is Greatest fills what is between the heavens and the earth, and prayer is light, and charity is proof, and patience is radiance, and the Qur'an is a proof for you or against you, and every person goes out, so he sells himself, freeing it, or selling it, destroying it. And the wording is of the hadith of Musa ibn Ismail. And Muslim said in his hadith: There is no god but Allah and Allah is Greatest fills what is between the heaven and the earth."
"3423","3424 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam informed me, from his brother Zayd ibn Sallam, from his grandfather Abu Sallam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Purity is half of faith, and praise be to Allah fills the scale, and glory be to Allah and Allah is Greatest fills what is between the heaven and the earth, and prayer is light, and charity is proof, and patience is radiance."
"3424","3425 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, (h). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Musa ibn Khalaf narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (h). And Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, both saying: Musa ibn Khalaf al-Ammi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from his grandfather Mamtur, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four remain in my ummah of the affair of ignorance, they shall not leave them: boasting of lineages, reviling of ancestors, seeking rain by the stars, and wailing, and the wailing woman, if she does not repent before she dies, shall come on the Day of Resurrection with a garment of tar and a coat of the flame of the Fire. He said: So Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: We left wailing when we left al-Lat and al-Uzza."
"3425","3426 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it, except that he said: And a coat of mange. Muslim did not mention in his hadith the speech of Umar."
"3426","3427 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Musa ibn Khalaf narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from his grandfather Mamtur, from al-Harith al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, commanded Yahya ibn Zakariya with five words to act upon them, and to command the Children of Israel to act upon them, and he was about to delay, so Isa said to him: You have been commanded with five words to act upon them and to command the Children of Israel to act upon them, so either you command them, or I shall command them. So he said: Do not do, O my brother, for I fear if you precede me to them that I be punished or swallowed. So he gathered the people in Bayt al-Maqdis until it was full, and they sat upon the balconies, so he praised Allah and extolled Him, then admonished them and said: Allah, mighty and majestic, commanded me with five words, to act upon them and to command you to act upon them. The first of them: That you worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, and the like of that is like a man who bought a slave from his pure wealth with gold or silver, and said: This is my house and this is my work, so work and render your work to me, but he worked and rendered his work to other than his master, so which of you would be pleased that his slave be thus, working and rendering his work to other than him? And Allah created you and provided for you, so worship Him and associate nothing with Him. And He commanded you with prayer, so when you pray, do not turn away, for Allah, mighty and majestic, sets His face toward the face of His servant so long as he does not turn away. And He commanded you with fasting, and the like of that is like a man with a group having a bundle of musk, all of them love to find its scent, and the mouth of the fasting person is more fragrant to Allah than the scent of musk. And He commanded you with charity, and the like of that is like one whom the enemy captured, tying his hand to his neck and bringing him near to strike his neck, so he said: I shall ransom myself from you, and kept giving little and much until he freed himself from them. And He commanded you with much remembrance of Allah, and the like of the remembrance of Allah, mighty and majestic, is like a man whom the enemy sought swiftly in his tracks, so he came to a fortified fortress and secured himself in it, and the most secure the servant is from Satan is when he is in the remembrance of Allah, exalted. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said thereupon: And I command you with five, Allah commanded me with them: the community, hearing, obedience, emigration, and striving in the path of Allah; so whoever separates from the community a handspan has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck unless he returns, and whoever calls with the call of ignorance is of the scum of Hell. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he fasts and prays? He said: Even if he fasts and prays."
"3427","3428 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from his grandfather Mamtur, from al-Harith al-Ash'ari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, mighty and majestic, commanded Yahya ibn Zakariya with five words to act upon them and to command the Children of Israel to act upon them. Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Musa ibn Khalaf."
"3428","3429 - Abu Husayn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from his grandfather Mamtur, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"3429","3430 - Muhammad ibn Abdah al-Missisi narrated to us, Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from Abu Sallam, al-Harith al-Ash'ari narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, commanded Yahya ibn Zakariya with five words to act upon them and to command the Children of Israel to act upon them, and he delayed, so Isa said to him: You have been commanded with five words to act upon them and to command the Children of Israel to act upon them, so either you command them with them, or I shall stand and command them with them. Yahya said: If you precede me with them I fear I shall be punished or swallowed, so he gathered the Children of Israel in Bayt al-Maqdis until the mosque was full and the people sat upon the balconies, so he admonished the people then said: Allah commanded me with five words to act upon them and to command you to act upon them. The first of them: That you associate nothing with Allah, for whoever associates anything with Allah, his like is like a man who bought a slave from his pure wealth with gold or silver, and said: This is my house and my work, so render your work, but he worked and rendered his work to other than his master, so which of you loves that he have a slave thus rendering his work to other than his master, and Allah, mighty and majestic, He created you and provided for you, so associate nothing with Allah. And Allah commanded you with prayer, so when you set your faces, do not turn away, for Allah, mighty and majestic, sets His face toward the face of His servant when he stands praying, and does not turn His face from him until the servant himself turns. And He commanded you with fasting, for the like of the fasting person is like a man with a bundle of musk among a group, none of them having musk but he, all of them desire to find its scent, and the breath of the fasting person's mouth is more fragrant to Allah than the scent of musk. And He commanded you with charity, for its like is like a man whom the enemy took and captured, tying his hand to his neck and bringing him forward to strike his neck, so he said: Do not kill me, for I shall ransom myself from you with such-and-such wealth, so they released him, and he kept gathering for them until he ransomed himself; thus is charity, by it the servant ransoms himself from the punishment of Allah. And He commanded you with much remembrance of Allah, and the like of that is like a man wronged by the enemy who hastened in his pursuit, and he went until he came to a fortified fortress and secured himself in it; thus is Satan, the servants secure themselves from him only by the remembrance of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I command you with five words Allah commanded me with them: the community, hearing, obedience, emigration, and striving in the path of Allah; so whoever leaves the community a handspan has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck unless he returns, and whoever calls with the call of ignorance is of the scum of Hell. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he prays and fasts? He said: Yes, even if he prays and fasts, so call with the call of Allah by which He named you Muslims, believers, servants of Allah."
"3430","3431 - Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir al-Anbari narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from his grandfather, al-Harith al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not command you with five words Allah, mighty and majestic, commanded me with them? The community, hearing, obedience, emigration, and striving in the path of Allah; so whoever leaves the community a handspan has cast off the yoke of Islam from his head unless he returns, and whoever calls with the call of ignorance is of the scum of Hell. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he fasts and prays? He said: Even if he fasts and prays, call with the call of Allah by which He named you Muslims, believers, servants of Allah."
"3431","Ibrahim ibn Muqsim, freedman of Hudhayl, from Abu Malik. 3432 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Ayyash ibn Abbas, from Ibrahim ibn Miqsam, freedman of Hudhayl, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that he came with his companions in a ship, with a piebald horse with him, and when they were sent they found many camels of the camels of the polytheists and took them, so Abu Malik ordered them to slaughter a camel of them and seek help with it, then went on foot until he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and informed him of his journey and his companions and the camels they had taken, then returned to his companions, so those with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give us, O Messenger of Allah, of these camels. So he said: Go to Abu Malik. When they came to him he divided them into fifths: a fifth he sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and took a third of the remainder after the fifth and divided it among his companions, and the remaining two-thirds among the Muslims, divided among them, so they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We have seen nothing like what Abu Malik did with this booty. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I been, I would have done only as he did."
"3432","Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari. 3433 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ibn Abi Husayn, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this verse was revealed: Do not ask about things which, if made manifest to you, would distress you. He said: So we were asking him when he said: Allah has servants who are neither prophets nor martyrs, envied by the prophets and martyrs for their nearness and seat from Allah, mighty and majestic, on the Day of Resurrection. He said: And in the side of the people was a Bedouin, so he stood and knelt upon his knees and threw with his hands, then said: Tell us, O Messenger of Allah, of them, who are they? He said: So I saw the face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brighten, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Servants of the servants of Allah from various lands and tribes of the peoples of the wombs of tribes, between whom were no kinships by which they kept ties for Allah, no worldly goods they exchanged for it, loving one another by the spirit of Allah, mighty and majestic; Allah makes their faces light, makes for them pulpits of pearl before the Most Merciful, exalted; the people panic and they do not panic, and the people fear and they do not fear."
"3433","3434 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Malik ibn Su'ayr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shimmer ibn Atiyyah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Servants of Allah for whom pulpits of light shall be placed on the Day of Resurrection, who are neither prophets nor martyrs, envied by the prophets and martyrs. They said: So who are they? He said: Those who love one another for Allah, mighty and majestic."
"3434","3435 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Abu al-Minhal, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, who said: There was a man of us who had accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), called Malik or Abu Malik, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I have known peoples who are neither prophets nor martyrs, envied by the prophets and martyrs, as though they are of Allah, mighty and majestic, peoples of various tribes loving one another for Allah."
"3435","3436 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, placing the men next to him, and placing the boys behind that, and placing the women behind that."
"3436","3437 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in all of them, meaning the four of Zuhr and Asr."
"3437","Shurayh ibn Ubayd al-Hadrami from Abu Malik. 3438 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti and Abu Zayd al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, that Abu Malik al-Ash'ari said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The sweetness of the world is the bitterness of the Hereafter, and the bitterness of the Hereafter is the sweetness of the world."
"3438","3439 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three men: one had ten dinars and gave a dinar of them in charity, another had ten uqiyyahs and gave an uqiyyah of them in charity, and another had a hundred uqiyyahs and gave ten uqiyyahs in charity. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are equal in reward; each has given a tenth of his wealth in charity. Allah, mighty and majestic, said: Let the one of means spend of his means."
"3439","3440 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has protected you from three traits: that your Prophet supplicate against you and you perish all together, that the people of falsehood prevail over the people of truth, and that you unite upon misguidance; from these Allah has protected you, and your Lord has warned you of three: the Smoke, which seizes the believer like a cold, and seizes the disbeliever, swelling him, coming out of every hearing organ of his, the second the Beast, and the third the Dajjal."
"3440","3441 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man sneezes let him say: Praise be to Allah in every state, and let those around him say: May Allah have mercy on you, and let him say to those around him: May Allah guide you and set right your state."
"3441","3442 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I fear for my ummah only three traits: that wealth be multiplied for them, so they envy and fight one another, that the Books be opened for them, the believer taking to seek its interpretation, while none knows its interpretation but Allah, and those firm in knowledge saying: We believe in it, all is from our Lord, and none remembers but those of understanding, and that they see their learned one and neglect him, not caring for him."
"3442","3443 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not associate anything with Allah after having believed in Him, establishes the prescribed prayer, pays the obligatory zakat, fasts Ramadan, hears and obeys, then dies upon that, Paradise is incumbent for him."
"3443","3444 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the Farewell Pilgrimage, in the days of sacrifices, to the people: Is not this the sacred day? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then the sanctity of what is between you until the Day of Resurrection is like the sanctity of this day, and shall I tell you who is the Muslim? The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and shall I tell you who is the believer? One whom the Muslims trust over themselves and their wealth, and shall I tell you who is the emigrant? One who abandons evil deeds, and the believer is forbidden to the believer like the sanctity of this day; his flesh is forbidden to him to eat by backbiting him, and his honor is forbidden to him to violate, and his face is forbidden to him to strike, and his blood is forbidden to him to shed, and his wealth is forbidden to him to wrong, and harming him is forbidden to him, and it is forbidden to him to push him away with a push."
"3444","3445 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your enemy is not one whom, if you kill him, is light for you, and if he kills you, you enter Paradise, but your most hostile enemy is your child who came from your loins, then your most hostile enemy is your wealth which your right hand possesses."
"3445","3446 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Trial shall be sent, and with it caprice and patience shall be sent; so whoever follows caprice, his killing is black, and whoever follows patience, his killing is white."
"3446","3447 - Hashim ibn Marthad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three traits I have concealed from My servants; had they seen them they would never do evil ever: Had I uncovered My veil so they saw Me until they were certain and knew how I deal with My creation when I give them death and grasp the heavens in My hand, then grasp the earth and the earths, then say: I am the King; who is it that has dominion besides Me? Then I showed them Paradise and what I have prepared for them therein of every good, so they were certain of it, and showed them the Fire and what I have prepared for them of every evil, so they were certain of it, but deliberately I concealed that from them, to know how they act though I have made it clear to them."
"3447","3448 - Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man who wakes in the night and wakes his wife, and if sleep overcomes her he sprinkles water upon her face, then they stand in their house remembering Allah, mighty and majestic, an hour of the night, but they are forgiven."
"3448","3449 - Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most faithful word with Allah is that the servant say: O Allah, You are my Lord and I am Your servant; I have wronged myself and confessed my sin, and none forgives sins but You; O Lord, forgive me."
"3449","3450 - Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to say when we wake, when we evening, and when we lie upon our beds: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, You are the Lord of all things, and the angels bear witness that there is no god but You, so we seek refuge in You from the evil of ourselves, and from the evil of the accursed Satan and his association, and that we commit evil against ourselves or bring it to a Muslim."
"3450","3451 - Hashim ibn Marthad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the son of Adam sleeps, the angel says to Satan: Give me your scroll, so he gives it to him, and whatever good he finds in his scroll, he erases with it ten evils from the scroll of Satan and writes them as good deeds; so when one of you wishes to sleep, let him utter takbir thirty-three times, and praise thirty-four praises, and glorify thirty-three glorifications, making a hundred."
"3451","3452 - Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam narrated to me, from Shurayh, from Abu Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: When a man enters his house let him say: O Allah, I ask You the good of entering and the good of leaving; in the name of Allah we enter, and in the name of Allah we leave, and upon Allah our Lord we rely, then he greets himself."
"3452","3453 - Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes let him say: We have woken and sovereignty belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds; O Allah, I ask You the good of this day, its opening, its victory, its light, its blessing and its guidance, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what is in it and the evil of what is before it and the evil of what is after it, then when he evenings let him say the like of that."
"3453","3454 - Hashim ibn Marthad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let one of you say when he wishes to sleep: I believe in Allah and disbelieve in the false deity; the promise of Allah is true and the messengers spoke the truth; O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the night-comers of this night, except a comer that comes with good."
"3454","3455 - Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam narrated to me, from Shurayh, from Abu Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, there shall surely be raised of you on the Day of Resurrection to Paradise like the black night, a company all of whom encompass the earth; the angels say: Those who came with Muhammad are more than those who came with the prophets."
"3455","3456 - Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam narrated to me, from Shurayh, from Abu Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, does not look at your bodies nor at your lineages nor at your wealth, but looks at your hearts; so whoever has a righteous heart, Allah is compassionate to him, and you are but the children of Adam, and the most beloved of you to me is the most God-fearing of you."
"3456","3457 - Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make death beloved to one who knows that I am Your Messenger."
"3457","3458 - Hashim ibn Marthad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The promised day is the Day of Resurrection, and the witness is Friday, and the witnessed is the day of Arafah, and Friday Allah stored for us, and the middle prayer is the Asr prayer."
"3458","3459 - Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam narrated to me, from Shurayh, from Abu Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Friday is expiation for what is between it and the Friday before it, plus three days, and that is because Allah, mighty and majestic, said: Whoever comes with a good deed shall have ten like it."
"3459","3460 - Hashim ibn Marthad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayers are expiations for what is between them, for Allah, mighty and majestic, said: Good deeds remove evil deeds."
"3460","3461 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Urwah al-Himsi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Damdam ibn Zur'ah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are a shown-mercy, pardoned ummah, so be upright and take the capacity of the affair."
"3461","Khalid ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Abu Malik. 3462 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard Abu Malik al-Ash'ari saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the Farewell Pilgrimage, in the middle of the days of sacrifice: Is not this the sacred day? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then the sanctity between you until the Day of Resurrection is like the sanctity of this day. Then he said: Shall I not tell you who is the Muslim? One from whose tongue the Muslims are safe, and shall I tell you who is the believer? One whom the believers trust over themselves and their blood, and shall I tell you who is the emigrant? One who abandons evil deeds and abandons what Allah has forbidden; the believer is forbidden to the believer like the sanctity of this day; his flesh is forbidden to him to eat and backbite him in absence, and his honor is forbidden to him to violate, and his face is forbidden to him to strike, and it is forbidden to him to push him with a push that wrongs him."
"3462","Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari. 3463 - Hafs al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, (h). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, both from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The greatest misappropriation with Allah on the Day of Resurrection is a cubit of land - or he said: a handspan - which a man or neighbor steals, when there is land between them, and one of them steals it from his fellow; so he is collared with it of seven earths."
"3463","Mu'aniq, or Abu Mu'aniq, or Ibn Mu'aniq, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari; thus is his name reported with doubt. 3464 - Ismail ibn Qirat al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Yusuf, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Sallam, from Ibn Mu'aniq al-Dimashqi, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever establishes prayer and pays zakat and dies worshipping Allah, associating nothing with Him, it is indeed incumbent upon Allah, mighty and majestic, to admit him to Paradise, whether he emigrated or sat in his birthplace. So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, if I tell the people of it they shall feel reassured by it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has prepared for the strivers in His path a hundred degrees, between every two degrees as between the heaven and the earth; had I what to strengthen myself with and strengthen the Muslims, or they had in their hands what to spend, no detachment would set out but I was its companion, but that is neither in my hand nor in their hands, and had I gone out, none in whom is good would remain but went out with me, and that is hard upon me, so I wish I would strive and be killed, then be given life, then strive and be killed, then be given life and be killed."
"3464","3465 - Ismail ibn Qirat al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Yusuf, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Sallam, from Ibn Mu'aniq al-Dimashqi, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever asks Allah for killing in His path sincerely from himself, then dies or is killed, he has the reward of a martyr, and whoever is wounded in the path of Allah or suffers a mishap, it shall come on the Day of Resurrection at its fullest as it was, its color like saffron and its scent the scent of musk, and whoever has wounds in the path of Allah has upon him the seal of the martyrs."
"3465","3466 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Mu'aniq or Abu Mu'aniq, from Abu Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise is a chamber whose outside is seen from its inside and its inside from its outside; Allah has prepared it for one who feeds food, softens speech, follows prayer, and stands by night while the people sleep."
"3466","3467 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, (h). And Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, both saying: Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, Abu Sallam narrated to me, Abu Mu'aniq al-Ash'ari narrated to me, Abu Malik al-Ash'ari narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise are chambers whose outside is seen from their inside and their inside from their outside; Allah, mighty and majestic, has prepared them for one who feeds food, fasts continually, and prays by night while the people sleep."
"3467","Ata al-Khurasani from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari. 3468 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Jabalah, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, commanded me to command you with five words: upon you is striving, hearing, obedience, and emigration; so whoever separates from the community a bow's length, neither prayer nor fasting is accepted from him, and those are the fuel of the Fire."
"3468","304 - Hurayth ibn Ghanim al-Shaybani. 3469 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Mu'ammar ibn Amr al-Mazini al-Basri narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Hassan al-Anbari narrated to us, my two grandmothers narrated to me, from their grandmother Qaylah bint Makhramah, who said: I went out seeking companionship to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I went in the morning to Hurayth ibn Ghanim and asked him for companionship, and he agreed, so I accompanied him, and we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying the dawn prayer, with the stars intertwined in the sky."
"3469","305 - Hurayth Abu Amr al-Makhzumi, and he is Hurayth ibn Amr ibn Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Makhzum. 3470 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truffle is of the manna, and its water is a cure for the eye."
"3470","306 - Hurayth ibn Zayd ibn Tha'labah al-Ansari, a Badri. 3471 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Luhay'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then among Banu Jusham ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Hurayth ibn Zayd ibn Tha'labah."
"3471","3472 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then among Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Hurayth ibn Zayd ibn Tha'labah ibn Abd al-Rabb."
"3472","307 - Harmalah ibn Amr al-Aslami. 3473 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Ibn Harmalah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Hind, from Harmalah ibn Amr, who said: I performed hajj with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Farewell Pilgrimage, while I was a boy with my uncle mounting me behind him, so I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing one of his fingers upon the other, so I said to my uncle: What is he saying? He said: He is saying: Stone the jamrahs with the like of the pebbles of khadhf."
"3473","3474 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah narrated to me, Yahya ibn Hind narrated to me, from my father Harmalah ibn Amr, that he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafah with my uncle mounting me behind him, so I looked at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his fingers one upon the other. He said: I said: What is he saying? He said: He is saying: Stone with the like of the pebbles of khadhf."
"3474","308 - Harmalah ibn Zayd al-Ansari. 3475 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Abu Dhubhah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Harmalah ibn Zayd came to him and sat before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, faith is here, pointing with his hand to his tongue, and hypocrisy is here, pointing with his hand to his chest, and he remembers Allah only a little. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent toward him, and he repeated that to him and Harmalah was silent, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the tip of the tongue of Harmalah and said: O Allah, make for him a truthful tongue, and a grateful heart, and grant him my love and the love of those who love me, and turn his affair to good. So Harmalah said: O Messenger of Allah, I have hypocrite brothers among whom I was a chief; shall I not point them out to you? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No; whoever comes to us as you have come to us, we seek forgiveness for him as we sought forgiveness for you, and whoever persists upon his sin, Allah is more entitled to him, and do not tear a veil from anyone."
"3475","309 - Harmalah Abu Ulaybah al-Anbari. 3476 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, my father narrated to us, and my uncle Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh, both saying: My father narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Dirghamah ibn Ulaybah ibn Harmalah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, who said: I set out in the delegation of the tribe to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he prayed with us the dawn prayer, and when he greeted I looked at the face of the one beside me, hardly recognizing him due to the darkness, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Fear Allah, and if you are among the people and hear them saying to you what pleases you, do it, and if you hear them saying to you what you dislike, leave it."
"3476","310 - Hidhyam Abu Hanzalah al-Hanafi. 3477 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, Dhayyal ibn Ubayd narrated to us, who said: I heard my grandfather saying: His father Hidhyam said: O Messenger of Allah, I have sons and this is my youngest son, so invoke blessing upon him. So he said: Come, O boy, and took my hand and wiped my head and said: May Allah bless you in him. He said: So I saw Hanzalah: a swollen man would be brought to him and he would wipe his hand upon him and say: In the name of Allah, and the swelling would go."
"3477","311 - Hidhyam ibn Amr al-Sa'di. 3478 - Abbad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Jarir informed us, (h). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ishaq al-Talqani narrated to us, (h). And Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (h). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani and Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Musa ibn Ziyad ibn Hidhyam ibn Amr al-Sa'di, from his father, from his grandfather Hidhyam ibn Amr, that he witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage, saying: Verily your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours in this land of yours. Have I not conveyed? They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness. And the wording is of the hadith of Abu al-Rabi'."
"3478","312 - Habbah and Sawa, the two sons of Khalid, of Banu Amr ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah ibn Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah. 3479 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sallam Abu Shurahbil, from Habbah and Sawa, the two sons of Khalid, both saying: We entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was treating something and we helped him, so he said: Do not despair of provision so long as your heads shake, for man is born of his mother red with no skin upon him, then Allah provides for him."
"3479","3480 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (h). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sallam Abu Shurahbil, from Habbah and Sawa, the two sons of Khalid, both saying: We entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Do not despair of provision so long as your heads shake, for man is born of his mother red with no skin upon him, then Allah, mighty and majestic, provides for him."
"3480","313 - Habbah ibn Juwayn al-Urani; it is said he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 3481 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu al-Miqdam, from Habbah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Ali, I enjoin upon you good toward the Arabs; I enjoin upon you good toward the Arabs."
"3481","314 - Hamal ibn Malik ibn al-Nabighah al-Hudhali. He said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) stood on the pulpit and said: I adjure by Allah any man who heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) give judgment concerning the fetus. So Hamal ibn Malik ibn al-Nabighah al-Hudhali stood and said: O Commander of the Believers, I was between two neighbor-wives - meaning co-wives - and one of them struck the other with the pole of her tent, killing her and killing what was in her womb. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged concerning the fetus a ghurrah, a slave or slave-girl. Umar said: Allah is Greatest; had we not heard this we would not have judged otherwise. [isnad, via key 3481: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Ibn Uyaynah, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both)]."
"3482","3482 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla: my father narrated to me from Ibn Abi Layla from al-Hakam from Mujahid from al-Hudhali: he had a wife and married another over her, and the two co-wives became jealous, so the Hilaliyyah struck the Amiriyyah with my tent-pole of wood, and she miscarried a dead child. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: pay blood-money for him. Her guardian came and said: Should we pay blood-money for one who neither ate nor drank nor cried out, so the like of that goes unavenged? He said: the rhymed speech of the bedouins - yes, pay blood-money for him; in it is a ghurrah, a slave or a young slave-girl."
"3483","3483 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Ziyad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Qurashi from Abu Bakr al-Hanafi: Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us from Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali from Hamal ibn al-Nabighah: he had two wives, a Lihyaniyyah and a Muawiyyah of Banu Muawiyah ibn Zayd, and they met and quarreled jealously, so the Muawiyyah lifted a stone and threw it at the Lihyaniyyah while she was pregnant and full-term, killing her, and she delivered a boy. Hamal ibn Malik said to Imran ibn Uwaymir: pay me the blood-money of my wife. They brought the case to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The blood-money is upon the asabah (paternal kin), and for the miscarried fetus a ghurrah, a slave or slave-girl."
"3484","3484 - Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Yazid ibn Zuray from Saeed ibn Abi Arubah from Qatadah from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah: Hamal ibn Malik ibn al-Nabighah had under him two co-wives, Mulaykah and Umm Afif. One of them threw a stone at the other and it struck her front, and she delivered a dead fetus, and she died. That was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he placed her blood-money upon the folk of the killer, and for her fetus a ghurrah, a slave or slave-girl, or twenty camels or a hundred sheep. Her guardian said: By Allah, O Prophet of Allah, he neither ate nor drank nor cried out and raised his voice, so the like of that goes unavenged. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have nothing to do with the rhymed saj of the Jahiliyyah."
"3485","315 - Hanzalah ibn Abi Amir ibn al-Rahib al-Ansari then al-Awsi, washed by the angels, martyred on the day of Uhud. 3486 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani: my father narrated to me from Ibn Lahiah from Abu al-Aswad from Urwah: among the names of those martyred on the day of Uhud with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Hanzalah ibn Abi Amir ibn Sayfi ibn Numan, washed by the angels."
"3486","3486 - Narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi from Muhammad ibn Fulayh from Musa ibn Uqbah from Ibn Shihab: among the names of those martyred on the day of Uhud of the Ansar, then of Banu Zurayq: Hanzalah ibn Abi Amir, he whom the angels washed."
"3487","3487 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah from Yahya ibn Maeen from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata from Saeed ibn Abi Arubah from Qatadah from Anas, who said: The two tribes, al-Aws and al-Khazraj, boasted. Al-Aws said: of us are four; al-Khazraj said: of us are four. Al-Aws said: of us is one at whom the Throne of the Merciful shook, Sad ibn Muadh; of us is one whose testimony equals that of two men, Khuzaymah ibn Thabit; of us is one whom the angels washed, Hanzalah ibn al-Rahib; and of us is one whose flesh the wasps protected, Asim ibn Thabit ibn al-Aflah. Al-Khazraj said: of us are four who gathered the Quran in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), none other gathered it: Ubayy ibn Kab, Muadh ibn Jabal, Zayd ibn Thabit, and Abu Zayd. I said to Anas: who is Abu Zayd? He said: one of my uncles."
"3488","316 - Hanzalah ibn al-Rabi al-Usayyidi, the scribe. 3489 - Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri from Abu al-Zinad: al-Muraqqi ibn Sayfi narrated from Hanzalah the scribe, who said: We went on campaign with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and passed a woman slain with people crowded over her. They made way for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: She was not one to fight. Then he said: Go and catch up with Khalid ibn al-Walid and say: do not kill offspring nor a hireling."
"3489","3489 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Hudhayfah from Sufyan from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from al-Haytham ibn Hanash from Hanzalah the scribe, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he mentioned Paradise and Hell, and we were as if seeing with our eyes. I went out to my family and laughed with them, and something entered my heart. I met Abu Bakr (may Allah have mercy on him) and said: I have been hypocritical. He said: How so? I said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he mentioned Paradise and Hell and we were as if seeing with our eyes, then I came to my family and laughed with them. Abu Bakr said: We too do that. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: O Hanzalah, had you remained with your families as you are with me, the angels would shake hands with you on your beds and on the road. O Hanzalah, an hour and an hour."
"3490","3490 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Saeed ibn Abi Maryam from Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, and narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym, both saying: Sufyan narrated from Saeed al-Jurayri from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Hanzalah the scribe al-Usayyidi, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we mentioned Paradise and Hell until we were as if seeing with our eyes. I went to my family and children and laughed and played, then remembered the state we had been in. I went out and met Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: I have been hypocritical. Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We too do it. Hanzalah went and mentioned it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: O Hanzalah, had you remained as you are with me, the angels would shake hands with you on your beds or your roads or the like. O Hanzalah, an hour and an hour."
"3491","3491 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi from al-Salt ibn Masud from Jafar ibn Sulayman from Saeed al-Jurayri from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Hanzalah the scribe, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"3492","3492 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Ismail al-Adawi al-Basri from Amr ibn Marzuq: Imran al-Qattan informed us from Qatadah from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir from Hanzalah al-Usayyidi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you remained as you are with me, the angels would shade you with their wings."
"3493","3493 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, both saying: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated from Saeed ibn Abi Arubah from Qatadah from Hanzalah al-Usayyidi - and he was called the scribe of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guards the five prayers, or the prescribed prayer, with its ablution, its times, its bowing and its prostration, regarding it as a due upon him, Allah forbids him to the Fire."
"3494","3494 - Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni al-Tustari from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr from Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated from Saeed from Qatadah from Hanzalah al-Usayyidi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"3495","3495 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad from al-Nadr ibn Hammad al-Ataki: Sayf ibn Umar al-Usayyidi narrated from Muhammad ibn Nuwayrah from Abu Uthman from Ibn Abi Miknaf from Hanzalah the scribe: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali ibn Abi Talib and Khalid ibn al-Walid (may Allah be pleased with them both) to Yemen, saying: When you meet, Ali is the amir, and when you separate, each of you is over his own task. Khalid ibn al-Walid wrote to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) beginning with himself, and he did not object to that; and Ali wrote to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - may Allah be pleased with him - beginning with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). As in the print; the correct name is (Abu Uthman ibn Miknaf)."
"3496","3496 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah from Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Kisai from Ismail ibn Aban: Abu Hammad al-Hanafi narrated from Muhammad ibn Nuwayrah from Abu Uthman from Hanzalah ibn al-Rabi the scribe, who said: al-Muqawqis, king of the Copts, gifted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a gift and a white mule, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepted it."
"3497","317 - Hanzalah ibn Hidhaym ibn Jumuah al-Maliki. 3498 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami from Muhammad ibn Uthman: Dhayyal ibn Ubayd ibn Hanzalah narrated, saying: I heard my grandfather Hanzalah say: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him sitting cross-legged."
"3498","3498 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami from Muhammad ibn Uthman: Dhayyal ibn Ubayd ibn Hanzalah narrated, saying: I heard my grandfather Hanzalah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked to call a man by his most beloved names and his most beloved kunyahs."
"3499","3499 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami from Muhammad ibn Uthman: Dhayyal ibn Ubayd ibn Hanzalah narrated, saying: I heard my grandfather Hanzalah say: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have an orphan in my care and I gave him in charity a hundred camels. I saw anger in his face and he said: No; charity is only five, or else ten, or else fifteen, until it reaches forty."
"3500","3500 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami from Muhammad ibn Uthman: Dhayyal ibn Ubayd narrated, saying: I heard my grandfather say: His father Hidhaym said: O Messenger of Allah, I have many sons and this is my youngest, so bless him. He said: Come, boy. He took my hands, wiped my head and said: May Allah bless him. He said: I saw Hanzalah when a swollen man was brought to him; he would wipe his hand over him saying: In the name of Allah, and the swelling would go."
"3501","3501 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami from Salm ibn Qutaybah: Dhayyal ibn Ubayd narrated, saying: I heard my grandfather Hanzalah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no orphanhood after puberty, nor orphanhood for a girl when she menstruates."
"3502","318 - Hanzalah ibn al-Numan. 3503 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah from Dirar ibn Surad from Ali ibn Hashim from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi from his father, concerning the names of those who were with Ali among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Hanzalah ibn al-Numan."
"3503","319 - Hubshi ibn Junadah al-Saluli. 3504 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, and narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Ibn al-Asbahani, both saying: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated from Mujalid from al-Shabi from Hubshi ibn Junadah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while standing at Arafah in the Farewell Hajj when a bedouin came, took the edge of his cloak and asked him for it, and he gave it to him. Thereupon begging was forbidden. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for a rich man nor for one of sound strength except in grinding poverty or crushing debt. He said: Whoever begs people to increase his wealth, it will be scratches on his face and hot stones he eats from Hell; whoever wills, let him take little, and whoever wills, let him take much."
"3504","3504 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq from his father: Abu Hamzah narrated from al-Shabi from Hubshi ibn Junadah al-Saluli, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever begs people when not struck by calamity, it is as if he swallows a hot stone."
"3505","3505 - Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail: Israil narrated from Abu Ishaq from Hubshi ibn Junadah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever begs when not poor, it is as if he eats live coal."
"3506","3506 - Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab, and narrated Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani from Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali, and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Yahya al-Himmani, all saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated from Abu Ishaq from Hubshi ibn Junadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever begs when not poor, it is as if he eats from live coal."
"3507","3507 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Musa ibn al-Husayn Abu al-Husayn al-Saluli: Ghusn ibn Hammad narrated from Israil from Abu Ishaq from Hubshi ibn Junadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever begs when not poor, it is as if he eats live coal. Al-Hadrami said: Ghusn ibn Hammad is Ghusn ibn Muhammad ibn Yunus ibn Ishaq."
"3508","3508 - Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Abu Ghassan: Israil narrated from Abu Ishaq from Hubshi ibn Junadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. He said on the third or fourth time: and those who shorten."
"3509","3509 - Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab, and narrated Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani from Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali, and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Bilal al-Ashari, all saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated from Abu Ishaq from Hubshi ibn Junadah: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. It was said: and those who shorten? He said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. It was said: and those who shorten? He said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. He said on the fourth: and those who shorten."
"3510","3510 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, and narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr from Abu Ghassan, and narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qitrani from Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl, and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi, Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi and Yahya al-Himmani, all saying: Sharik narrated from Abu Ishaq from Hubshi ibn Junadah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Ali is from me and I am from him, and none discharges on my behalf except I and Ali. Ibn Abi Shaybah added in his hadith: Sharik said: I said: O Abu Ishaq, did you see him? He said: He stood among us in our gathering and narrated it to us."
"3511","3511 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Yahya al-Himmani, and narrated Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani from Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali, both saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated from Abu Ishaq from Hubshi ibn Junadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None settles my debt but I or Ali."
"3512","3512 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated from Abu Ishaq from Hubshi ibn Junadah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Ali is from me and I am from him, and none discharges on my behalf except I or Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"3513","3513 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Ali ibn Bahr: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated from Salman ibn Qarm al-Dabbi from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, who said: I heard Hubshi ibn Junadah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on the day of Ghadir Khumm: O Allah, whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him, aid whoever aids him and help whoever helps him. As in the print; the correct name is (Sulayman ibn Qarm)."
"3514","3514 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani from Ismail ibn Abd Allah al-Asbahani: Ismail ibn Aban narrated: Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated from Abu Ishaq from Hubshi ibn Junadah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa."
"3515","3515 - Narrated al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani from Ali ibn Musa ibn Ubayd al-Harithi al-Kufi: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated: Israil narrated from Abu Ishaq from Hubshi ibn Junadah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Unjust toll-taking is a form of wrongdoing."
"3516","320 - Habib ibn Maslamah al-Fihri, that is Habib ibn Maslamah ibn Malik ibn Wahb ibn Amr ibn Shayban ibn Muharib ibn Fihr ibn Malik. His mother was Fihriyyah. His kunyah Abu Abd al-Rahman, and he was called Habib of the Byzantines for his fighting them. 3517 - Narrated Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj from Yahya ibn Bukayr, who said: Habib ibn Maslamah died in the year forty-two at the age of fifty."
"3517","3517 - Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Saeed ibn Abd al-Aziz: Makhul narrated to him from Ziyad ibn Jariyah from Habib ibn Maslamah: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted a third after a fourth."
"3518","3518 - Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir from Makhul from Ziyad ibn Jariyah from Habib ibn Maslamah: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted a third after a fifth."
"3519","3519 - Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi: Sufyan narrated: Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir al-Azdi narrated from Makhul from Ziyad ibn Jariyah from Habib ibn Maslamah al-Fihri, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granting a third at the outset."
"3520","3520 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Mahfuz ibn Bahr al-Antaki, and narrated Musa ibn Harun from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Miqsami: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Ziyad ibn Sad from Yazid ibn Jabir from Makhul from Ziyad ibn Jariyah from Habib ibn Maslamah, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granting a third."
"3521","3521 - Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, and narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud from Asad ibn Musa: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid from Yazid from Makhul from Ziyad ibn Jariyah from Habib ibn Maslamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would grant a fourth at the outset and a third on the return."
"3522","3522 - Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratis from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated: Abu Wahb narrated to me from Makhul that he narrated to them that Ziyad ibn Jariyah narrated to them that Habib ibn Maslamah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted a fourth and a third."
"3523","3523 - Narrated Abu Abd al-Malik Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi al-Dimashqi and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi, both saying: Muhammad ibn Aidh narrated: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated: al-Ala ibn al-Harith and Abu Wahb narrated to us from Makhul: Ziyad ibn Jariyah narrated to me from Habib ibn Maslamah: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted a fourth of what the folk brought at the outset and on the return a third after the fifth."
"3524","3524 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati from Abd Allah ibn Salih: Muawiyah ibn Salih informed me from al-Ala ibn al-Harith from Makhul from Ziyad ibn Jariyah from Habib ibn Maslamah: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would grant, when setting out on campaign, a fourth after the fifth, and when returning, a third after the fifth."
"3525","3525 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili from Ghassan ibn al-Rabi: Ibn Thawban narrated from his father from Makhul from Ziyad ibn Jariyah from Habib ibn Maslamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted a third."
"3526","3526 - Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated from Makhul from Ibn Jariyah from Habib ibn Maslamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted at the outset a fourth and on the return a third."
"3527","3527 - Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri, and narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud from Asad ibn Musa, both saying: Sulayman ibn Musa al-Dimashqi narrated from Makhul from Ziyad ibn Jariyah from Habib ibn Maslamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would grant us at our outset a fourth and on the return a third."
"3528","3528 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari: Damrah ibn Rabiah narrated from Raja ibn Abi Salamah, who said: I heard Sulayman ibn Musa and Amr ibn Shuayb discuss the nafal in the Sacred Mosque. Amr said: There is no nafal after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Sulayman said to him: The folk of raisins at Taif kept you busy. Makhul narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Jariyah from Habib ibn Maslamah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted at the outset a fourth and on the return a third."
"3529","3529 - Narrated Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh: al-Walid ibn Muslim informed us from Saeed ibn Abd al-Aziz from Sulayman ibn Musa from Makhul from Ziyad ibn Jariyah from Habib ibn Maslamah, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granting at the outset a fourth and on the return a third."
"3530","3530 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Asbahani from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Shuayb ibn Ishaq al-Dimashqi: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir narrated from Makhul from Ziyad ibn Jariyah from Habib ibn Maslamah: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted at the outset a fourth and on the return a third."
"3531","3531 - Narrated Ali ibn Saeed al-Razi from Ali ibn Mabad ibn Nuh: Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd narrated: Saeed ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated from Atiyyah ibn Qays from Ziyad ibn Jariyah from Habib ibn Maslamah, who said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granting at his outset a fourth and on his return a third in a campaign."
"3532","3532 - Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi, all saying: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated: Amr ibn Waqid narrated: Musa ibn Yasar narrated to me from Makhul from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, who said: We camped at Dabiq under Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, and it reached Habib ibn Maslamah that Bannah, lord of Cyprus, had set out heading for the chief of Adharbayjan with emerald, ruby, pearl, gold and brocade borne on horses. He killed him and brought what was with him. Abu Ubaydah wanted to take a fifth of it, so Habib said: Do not deprive me of a provision Allah provided me; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the spoils for the killer. Muadh said: O Habib, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man has only what his imam willingly allows him."
"3533","3533 - Narrated Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Mulayl from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Umayyah al-Damri: Habib ibn Maslamah al-Qurashi met Qays ibn Sad ibn Ubadah while on a horse, so Habib ibn Maslamah stepped back from the saddle and said to Qays: Mount. Qays ibn Sad said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The owner of the mount is most entitled to its front. Habib said: I am not ignorant of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, but I fear for you."
"3534","3534 - Narrated Azhar ibn Zufar al-Misri from Abu Aslam Muhammad ibn Makhlad al-Ruayni: Sulayman ibn Abi Karimah narrated from Makhul from Qazaah ibn Yahya from Habib ibn Maslamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Visit occasionally and love will increase."
"3535","3535 - Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri: Ibn Lahiah narrated: Ibn Hubayrah narrated to me from Habib ibn Maslamah al-Fihri - and he was one whose supplication was answered - that he was put in command of an army and traversed the mountain passes. When he met the enemy he said to the people: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No gathering gathers and one of them supplicates while the rest say amin but Allah answers them. Then he praised Allah and extolled Him and said: O Allah, spare our blood and make our rewards the rewards of martyrs. While they were so, al-Hanbat, the enemy commander, descended and entered Habib's pavilion. Abu al-Qasim said: al-Hanbat in the Byzantine tongue is the commander of the army."
"3536","321 - Habib ibn Siba Abu Jumuah al-Ansari, and it is said: Junayd ibn Sab. 3537 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti and Abu Zayd al-Hawti, both saying: Abu al-Mughirah narrated: al-Awzai narrated: Asid ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me: Salih ibn Jubayr narrated to me: Abu Jumuah narrated to me, saying: We lunched with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and with us was Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. He said: O Messenger of Allah, is anyone better than us - we accepted Islam with you? He said: Yes, a folk who come after you believing in me though they never saw me."
"3537","3537 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti and Abu Zayd al-Hawti, both saying: Abu al-Mughirah narrated, and narrated Abu Shuayb al-Harrani from Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti, both saying: al-Awzai narrated: Asid ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me from Khalid ibn Durayk from Abu Muhayriz, who said: I said to Abu Jumuah: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes, I will narrate to you a fine hadith. We lunched with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and with us was Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. He said: O Messenger of Allah, is anyone better than us - we believed in you and strove with you? He said: A folk who come after you believing in me though they never saw me."
"3538","3538 - Narrated Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Qurashi from his father: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated: al-Awzai narrated: Abu Ubayd narrated from Salih ibn Jubayr from Abu Jumuah, who said: We campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and with us was Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. He said: Is anyone better than us, O Messenger of Allah - we accepted Islam, emigrated and strove with you? He said: Yes, a folk who come after me believing in me though they never saw me."
"3539","3539 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl from Abd Allah ibn Salih: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to me from Salih ibn Jubayr that he said: Abu Jumuah al-Ansari, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), came to us at Bayt al-Maqdis to pray in it, and with us was Raja ibn Haywah that day. When he left, we went out with him to escort him. When we wanted to part, he said: You have upon me a gift and a right, that I narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We said: Give it, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with us Muadh ibn Jabal, ten in all. We said: O Messenger of Allah, is there any folk greater in reward than us - we believed in you and followed you? He said: What prevents you from that, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among you and revelation coming to you from heaven? Rather, a folk to whom a book comes between two tablets, and they believe in it and act by what is in it - they are greater in reward than you, they are greater in reward than you, they are greater in reward than you."
"3540","3540 - Narrated Ali ibn Saeed al-Razi from Bishr ibn Abd al-Wahhab: Damrah ibn Rabiah narrated from Marzuq ibn Nafi from Salih ibn Jubayr from Abu Jumuah al-Kinani, who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, is anyone better than us? He said: A folk who come after you finding a book between two tablets, believing in it and affirming it - they are better than you."
"3541","3541 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah from Saeed ibn Abi Maryam: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Muhammad ibn Yazid from Abd Allah ibn Awf from Abu Jumuah Habib ibn Siba - and he was of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Maghrib and forgot Asr. He said to his Companions: Did you see me pray Asr? They said: No, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the muadhdhin, who called the adhan, then the iqamah, and he prayed Asr, shortening the first, then prayed Maghrib."
"3542","3542 - Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Daqqaq al-Baghdadi from Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki: Abu Saeed, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated from Hujr Abu Khalaf: Abd Allah ibn Awf narrated: I heard Abu Jumuah al-Ansari Junayd ibn Sab say: I fought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the morning as a disbeliever, and fought with him in the evening as a Muslim. We were three men and nine women, and concerning us was revealed: Had there not been believing men and believing women."
"3543","322 - Habib ibn Zayd ibn Asim ibn Amr al-Mazini. 3544 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: among the names of those who witnessed al-Aqabah of the Ansar, then of Banu al-Najjar: Nusaybah - Ibn Numayr said: the people say Nusaybah - and her sister, the two daughters of Kab ibn Amr; her husband Zayd ibn Asim; and her two sons Abd Allah ibn Zayd and Habib ibn Zayd, whom Musaylimah seized."
"3544","323 - Habib ibn Ishaq al-Ansari, brother of Balharith ibn al-Khazraj, and it is said Khubayb. 3545 - Narrated Musa ibn Zakariyya al-Tustari from Shabab al-Usfuri: Bakr ibn Sulayman narrated from Ibn Ishaq, and Wahb ibn Jarir from his father from Ibn Ishaq, who said: Abu Bakr stayed with Habib ibn Isaf, brother of Balharith ibn al-Khazraj, at al-Sunh; and it is said: rather he stayed with Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Abi Zuhayr, brother of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj."
"3545","324 - Habib ibn Furayk. 3546 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, both saying: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated: Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: a man of Salaman ibn Sad narrated to me from his mother that her maternal uncle Habib ibn Furayk narrated to her that his father took him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his eyes whitened, seeing nothing with them. He asked him what befell him. He said: I was leading a camel of mine and stepped on snake eggs, and my sight was struck. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) blew into his eye and he saw; I saw him threading a thread into a needle at eighty years old, though his eyes were whitened."
"3546","325 - Habib ibn Khirash al-Asari. 3547 - Narrated Abu Ubaydah Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-Askari from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Jabalah: Ubayd ibn Hunayn al-Tai narrated, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Habib ibn Khirash al-Asari narrate from his father that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Muslims are brothers; none has merit over another except by piety."
"3547","326 - Husayn ibn Awf al-Khathami. 3548 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Ibn al-Asbahani: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated from Muhammad ibn Kurayb from Ibn Abbas, who said: Husayn ibn Awf narrated to me that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: My father is a very old man upon whom is the Hajj of Islam, and he cannot travel except carried عرضا - shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He fell silent, then said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father."
"3548","3548 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Abdan ibn Ahmad, both saying: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated from Muhammad ibn Kurayb from his father from Ibn Abbas: Husayn ibn Awf narrated to me, saying: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father reached the time of Hajj and cannot perform Hajj except lying عرضا. He fell silent a while, then said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father."
"3549","3549 - Narrated Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar from Rawh ibn Ubadah, and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Hafs ibn Abd Allah al-Hulwani: Buhlul ibn Muwarriq narrated, and Musa ibn Harun narrated ...: Bakkar ibn Abd Allah al-Rabadhi narrated: my uncle Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to me from his brother Abd Allah ibn Ubaydah from Husayn ibn Awf, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is a very old, weak man who has done all the laws of Islam except Hajj, and cannot hold himself on a camel - shall I perform Hajj on behalf of my father? He said: Tell me, if your father had a debt would you settle it? I said: Yes. He said: The debt of Allah is most deserving of settlement."
"3550","327 - Husayn ibn Utbah Abu Imran ibn al-Husayn al-Khuzai; his Islam is disputed - it is said he accepted Islam, and it is said he died in disbelief; the correct view is that he accepted Islam. He said, via Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qitrani from Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani from Abu Muawiyah from Shabib ibn Shaybah from al-Hasan from Imran ibn al-Husayn [hadith text continues under key 3551]."
"3551","He said - Husayn, father of Imran ibn al-Husayn, al-Khuzai - came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while a polytheist and said: O Muhammad, Abd al-Muttalib was better to his folk than you. Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Shayban. [parallel isnads, via key 3551: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abd Allah ibn Raja, Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Khirash; and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah: Jarir narrated from Mansur from Ribi, who said: I was told that...]."
"3552","3552 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Suwayd ibn Saeed: Ali ibn Mushir narrated from Dawud ibn Abi Hind from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman from Imran ibn Husayn: his father came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while a polytheist and said: Tell me of a man who honors guests; then he mentioned the like of it."
"3553","328 - Husayn ibn Wahwah al-Ansari. 3554 - Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Umar ibn Zurarah al-Hadathi: Isa ibn Yunus narrated from Saeed ibn Uthman al-Balawi from Urwah ibn Saeed al-Ansari from his father from Husayn ibn Wahwah: when Talhah ibn al-Bara met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: O Messenger of Allah, command me as you like and I will not disobey any order of yours. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marveled at that, he being a boy, and said to him thereupon: Go and kill your father. He went out turning to do it, so he called him back and said to him: Come, for I was not sent to sever kinship. Talhah later fell ill, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came visiting him in winter, in cold and cloud. When he left he said to his family: I see only that death has come upon Talhah, so inform me of him that I may witness him and pray over him, and hasten him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had not reached Banu Salim ibn Awf before he died, and night fell. Among what Talhah said was: Bury me and join me to my Lord, mighty and majestic, and do not call the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for I fear the Jews lest he be harmed on my account. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed in the morning, so he came and stood at his grave, the people lining with him, then raised his hands and said: O Allah, meet Talhah while he laughs to You."
"3554","329 - Husayn al-Himmani, that is Husayn ibn Mushmit ibn Shaddad ibn al-Namir ibn Murrah ibn Habban. 3555 - Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi, and Musa ibn Zakariyya al-Saji narrated from Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi, both saying: Muhriz ibn Wazr ibn Imran ibn Shuayth ibn Asim ibn Husayn ibn Mushmit ibn Shaddad ibn al-Namir ibn Murrah ibn Habban narrated: Wazr narrated to me that his father Imran narrated to him that his father Shuayth narrated to him that his father Asim narrated to him that his father Husayn narrated to him that he came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), pledged him the pledge of Islam and gave him the charity of his wealth. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him several waters at al-Maruth and the ridge of Jarad, among them Usayhib, al-Maghirah, Ahwa, al-Thimad and al-Sadirah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stipulated upon Husayn ibn Mushmit, of what he granted, that its pasture not be damaged and its water not be sold; and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stipulated upon Husayn ibn Mushmit that he not sell his water nor withhold its surplus. Zuhayr ibn Asim ibn Husayn spoke verse [omitted: only one hemistich word preserved]."
"3555","330 - Husayn ibn al-Harith ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abd Manaf, a Badri. 3556 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, among the names of those who witnessed Badr: Husayn ibn al-Harith ibn Abd Manaf."
"3556","3556 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah from Dirar ibn Surad: Ali ibn Hashim narrated from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi from his father, among the names of those who were with Ali: Husayn ibn al-Harith, a Badri who witnessed with him all his battles, of Banu al-Muttalib ibn Abd Manaf."
"3557","332 - Husayn ibn Aws, and it is said Ibn Qays al-Nahshali. 3558 - Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from Musa ibn Ismail: Ghassan ibn al-Agharr al-Nahshali narrated: Ziyad ibn Husayn al-Nahshali narrated to me from his father Husayn ibn Aws: he came to Madinah with camels and said: O Messenger of Allah, order the folk of the valley to help me and treat me well. He ordered them, and they stood with him and treated him well. Then he called him, wiped his hand over his face and supplicated for him."
"3558","3558 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Sahl Abu Sahl al-Basri, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf, both saying: Abu al-Haytham Khalaf ibn al-Haytham al-Nahshali al-Qassar narrated: Ghassan ibn al-Agharr al-Nahshali narrated: my uncle Ziyad ibn Husayn narrated from his father Husayn ibn Qays: he carried food to Madinah and met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What do you carry, O bedouin? He said: Wheat. He said: What did you intend with it? He said: I intended to sell it. He wiped my head and said: Treat the bedouin well in trade."
"3559","3559 - Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Abd Allah ibn Muawiyah al-Jumahi: Nuaym ibn Husayn al-Sadusi narrated: my uncle narrated to me from my grandfather, who said: We came to Madinah with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) there, and with me were camels of mine. I said: O Messenger of Allah, order the folk of the open land to treat me well and help me. They stood with me. When I sold my camels I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said to me: Come near. He wiped his hand over my forelock and supplicated for me three times."
"3560","333 - Habis Abu Hayyah al-Tamimi. 3561 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Muadh al-Halabi from Abd Allah ibn Raja: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir: Hayyah ibn Habis al-Tamimi narrated to me that his father informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is nothing in omens from owls; the evil eye is real, and the truest of omens is the good omen."
"3561","3561 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir al-Anbari narrated: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir: Hayyah ibn Habis al-Tamimi narrated to me: my father narrated to me that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is nothing in omens from owls; the evil eye is real, and the truest of birds is the good omen."
"3562","334 - Habis ibn Rabiah al-Yamani. 3563 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun narrated from Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi Awn, who said: Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) passed on the day of Siffin leaning on al-Ashtar, and Habis passed - and Habis was of the worshippers - so al-Ashtar said: O Commander of the Believers, Habis is with them; my memory of him, by Allah, is as a believer. Ali said: Today he is a believer."
"3563","335 - Habis ibn Sad al-Tai. 3564 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti and Abu Zayd al-Hawti, both saying: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated: Hariz ibn Uthman narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ghabir al-Alhani, who said: Habis ibn Sad al-Tai, who had met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), entered the mosque before dawn with people praying in the front of the mosque. He said: Hypocrites, by the Lord of the Kabah - frighten them; whoever frightens them has obeyed Allah and His Messenger. He said: The angels pray before dawn in the front of the mosque."
"3564","336 - Hazim ibn Harmalah al-Ghifari. 3565 - Narrated Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri: my father narrated to me, and narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri, and narrated Masadah al-Attar al-Makki from Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, all saying: Muhammad ibn Man ibn Muhammad narrated from Khalid ibn Saeed al-Muzani from Abu Zaynab, freedman of Hazim ibn Harmalah: Hazim ibn Harmalah narrated to me, saying: I passed one day and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me. I came to him and he said: Say often: There is no might nor power except by Allah, for it is of the treasures of Paradise."
"3565","337 - Harb ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi. 3566 - Narrated Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi: Yala ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi narrated, saying: I heard al-Rabi ibn Ziyad from Harb ibn al-Harith, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the pulpit on Friday saying: We have ordered for women woad and needles; as for the woad, it came to them from Yemen, and as for the needles, taken from dhimmis of what is due of the jizyah. I said to al-Rabi - or it was said to him: Did al-Rabi ibn Harb hear it? He said: Yes."
"3566","338 - Hisl, brother of Banu Amir ibn Luayy. 3567 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah al-Asbahani from Amr ibn Malik al-Rasibi: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul narrated: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Sabrah narrated: al-Qasim ibn Abi Ashmat informed me: my father narrated to me from my grandfather Hisl, one of Banu Amir ibn Luayy, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed in his Hajj, we with him, by a man who had finished his Hajj. He said to him: Was your Hajj accepted? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Begin deeds anew."
"3567","339 - Husayl ibn Kharijah al-Ashjai. 3568 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti: Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated: Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated from Ibrahim ibn Huwaysah al-Harithi from Man ibn Juwayriyah from Husayl ibn Kharijah al-Ashjai, who said: I came to Madinah with merchandise to sell, and I was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I will make for you twenty sa of dates if you guide these companions of mine to the road of Khaybar. I did so. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Khaybar and conquered it, I came, and he gave me the twenty, then I accepted Islam."
"3568","340 - Hujr ibn Adi al-Kindi. 3569 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani: Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated: Sufyan narrated from Abu Ishaq, who said: I saw Hujr ibn Adi when Muawiyah seized him, saying: This is my pledge, I neither rescind it nor seek rescission, before Allah and men."
"3569","341 - Hujr ibn Qays, and it is said he is Hujr ibn Anbas al-Kindi. 3570 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar from Zayd ibn Akhzam: Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated from Musa ibn Qays from Hujr ibn Qays - and he had reached the Jahiliyyah - who said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) proposed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her). He said: She is yours on condition you treat her well."
"3570","3570 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym: Musa ibn Qays al-Hadrami narrated, saying: I heard Hujr ibn Anbas - who had eaten blood in the Jahiliyyah and witnessed with Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) al-Jamal and Siffin - say: Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) proposed to Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She is yours, O Ali."
"3571","342 - Hujayr Abu Makhshi. 3572 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari: al-Nadr ibn Muhammad narrated: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated: Makhshi ibn Hujayr narrated to me: my father narrated to me that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed in the Farewell Hajj saying: O people, what land is this? They said: A sacred land. He said: What month is this? They said: A sacred month. He said: What day is this? They said: A sacred day. He said: Indeed your blood, your wealth and your honors are sacred upon you as the sanctity of this day of yours, as this month of yours, as the sanctity of this land of yours. Let your witness convey to your absent. Do not return after me disbelievers striking one another's necks."
"3572","343 - Hayyan Abu Imran al-Ansari. 3573 - Narrated Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi from his father, and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Saeed ibn Amr al-Ashathi, both saying: Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated from Humayd ibn Ali al-Raqashi from Imran ibn Hayyan al-Ansari from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed on the day of Khaybar and forbade them to sell a share of spoils before division, to have intercourse with pregnant women before they deliver, and fruit before its soundness appears and it is safe from blight. Duhaym added in his hadith: He permitted them three things he had forbidden: he permitted sacrificial meats, visiting graves, and vessels."
"3573","344 - Habban ibn Munqidh al-Ansari. 3574 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih from Amr ibn al-Rabi ibn Tariq: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated from Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Haywil from Ibn Shihab from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from his father from his grandfather Habban ibn Munqidh: a man said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I make a third of my prayer upon you? He said: Yes if you wish. He said: Two thirds? He said: Yes. He said: All my prayer? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then Allah will suffice you what concerns you of your world and Hereafter."
"3574","345 - Hayyan ibn Buh al-Sudai. 3575 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi from al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab: Ibn Lahiah narrated: Bakr ibn Sawadah narrated from Ziyad ibn Nuaym from Hayyan ibn Buh al-Sudai, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: My folk disbelieved and I was told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prepared an army against them. I came to him and said: My folk are upon Islam. He said: Is that so? I said: Yes. I followed him that night till morning and called the adhan for prayer. In the morning he gave me a vessel and I performed ablution in it; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his fingers in the vessel and springs gushed. He said: Whoever of you wants to perform ablution, let him. I performed ablution and prayed. He put me in command over them and gave me their charity. A man stood to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: So-and-so wronged me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no good in command for a Muslim man. Then a man came asking for charity, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is a headache, burning in the belly, and disease. So I gave him my document of command and charity. He said: What is the matter with you? I said: How can I accept it when I heard from you what I heard? He said: It is as you heard."
"3575","346 - Hayyan ibn Abjar al-Kinani; it is said he has companionship. 3576 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Saeed ibn Yahya ibn Saeed al-Umawi from his father from al-Amash, who said: I heard Hayyan, grandfather of Ibn Abjar the elder, say: Leave medicine while your body can bear the ailment."
"3576","3576 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Harun ibn Ishaq: Waki narrated from Israil from Jabir from Abd Allah ibn Yahya al-Hadrami: Hayyan ibn Abjar al-Kinani stripped the garments from a woman's belly until he treated her."
"3577","347 - Hariz or Abu Hariz, and it is said: Jarir or Abu Jarir. 3578 - Narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi from Asim ibn Ali, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani, both saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah from Ibn Abi Layla, who said: The lord of this house, Hariz or Abu Hariz, narrated to me, saying: When I reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was addressing, I placed my hands on the saddle-blanket of his mount and found it of ewe hide. As in the print and manuscript; the correct is (Abu Layla) as in Majma al-Zawaid, and Allah knows best."
"3578","348 - Hassan ibn Thabit al-Ansari, kunyah Abu al-Walid; he is Hassan ibn Thabit ibn Amr ibn Zayd ibn Adi ibn al-Najjar ibn Thalabah ibn Amr ibn al-Khazraj. 3579 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi from Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham: Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakkai narrated from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: Hassan ibn Thabit died in the year fifty-four."
"3579","3579 - Narrated Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Waqid al-Baghdadi from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah al-Harawi: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated from his father from Urwah from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her): the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would place for Hassan ibn Thabit a pulpit in the mosque upon which he recited poetry. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, aid him with the Holy Spirit as long as he defends Your Prophet."
"3580","3580 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn al-Dumayk from Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan: Ismail ibn Mujalid narrated from Hilal al-Wazzan from Urwah from Aishah: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed for Hassan a pulpit upon which he recited satire of the polytheists."
"3581","3581 - Narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi from Abd Allah ibn Salih: al-Layth narrated to me: Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to me from Saeed ibn Abi Hilal from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Aishah: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satirize Quraysh, for it is harder upon them than the shower of arrows. He sent to Ibn Rawahah saying: Satirize them; he satirized them but did not satisfy. He sent to Kab ibn Malik, then sent to Hassan ibn Thabit. When Hassan entered he said: It is time you sent to this lion lashing with his tail. Then he stuck out his tongue and moved it. He said: By Him who sent you with the truth, I will tear them as hide is torn. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not hasten, for Abu Bakr knows Quraysh lineages best, and I have kinship among them, until your knowledge of my lineage is clear. Hassan went to him then returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, your lineage is now clear to me; by Him who sent you with the truth, I will draw you out from them as a hair is drawn from dough. Aishah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to Hassan: The Holy Spirit still aids you as long as you defend Allah and His Messenger. She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Hassan satirized them and healed and was healed. Hassan said: [verse fragment as preserved]."
"3582","3582 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Muhammad ibn al-Abbas, Ishaq ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai al-Makki and Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani, all saying: al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated: Abu Ghaziyyah Muhammad ibn Musa narrated: Abd Allah ibn Musab narrated from Hisham ibn Urwah from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir from her grandmother Asma bint Abi Bakr, who said: al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam (may Allah be pleased with him) passed a gathering of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with Hassan ibn Thabit reciting his poetry to them while they were not eager for what they heard from him. Al-Zubayr sat with them and said: Why do I see you not listening to the poetry of Ibn al-Furayyah? He would present it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who would listen well and reward him amply, never distracted from him. Hassan said: Muhajjal [single word preserved]."
"3583","What Hassan ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) transmitted. 3584 - Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Ibn al-Musayyib: Hassan ibn Thabit was in a circle with Abu Hurayrah among them, and said to him: I adjure you by Allah, O Abu Hurayrah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Answer on my behalf; may Allah aid you with the Holy Spirit? He said: O Allah, yes."
"3584","3584 - Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Ibn al-Musayyib, who said: Hassan recited in the mosque and Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) passed and glanced at him. He said: In the mosque? In the mosque? He said: By Allah, I recited in it before one better than you; he feared he would allude to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he let him pass and left him."
"3585","3585 - Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from al-Qanabi and Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated from al-Zuhri from Saeed ibn al-Musayyib, who said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) passed Hassan while he recited in the mosque and glanced at him; then he mentioned the like of it."
"3586","3586 - Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Tawil: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Umar came upon Hassan ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with them both) while he recited in the mosque and said: Here? He said: I used to recite in it before one better than you. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) turned away fearing he would say the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Hassan turned to Abu Hurayrah and said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Hassan, answer on behalf of the Messenger of Allah; O Allah, aid him with the Holy Spirit? He said: Yes."
"3587","3587 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, and narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Sulayman ibn Harb and Amr ibn Marzuq; Hajjaj and Sulayman said: Shubah narrated, and Amr ibn Marzuq said: Shubah informed me, from Adi ibn Thabit from al-Bara: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hassan: Satirize them, and Jibril is with you."
"3588","3588 - Narrated al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazigh: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated: Shubah narrated from Adi ibn Thabit: al-Bara narrated to me, saying: I heard Hassan ibn Thabit say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Satirize them - meaning the polytheists - for Jibril is with you."
"3589","3589 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym, and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Ahmad ibn Yunus, both saying: Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated: Adi ibn Thabit narrated to me from al-Bara, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hassan: The Holy Spirit is with you as long as you satirize them - meaning the polytheists."
"3590","3590 - Narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi from Qabisah ibn Uqbah, and narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Saeed ibn Abi Maryam from Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, both saying: Sufyan narrated from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym from Abd al-Rahman ibn Bahman from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan ibn Thabit from his father: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed women who visit graves."
"3591","3591 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb and Husayn ibn Abd al-Awwal, both saying: Ubayd ibn Saeed al-Qurashi narrated: al-Thawri narrated from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym from Abd al-Rahman ibn Bahman from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan ibn Thabit from his father: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed women who visit graves."
"3592","3592 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar: Yahya ibn Muhammad, meaning al-Jari of the folk of al-Jar of the Madinah coast, narrated to me: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Musayyibi narrated to me from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from al-Araj from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan from his father Hassan ibn Thabit, who said: A need arose for us, the Ansar, before the governor, sought through a difficult matter. We walked to him with men of Quraysh and others; they spoke to him and mentioned to him the bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning us. He mentioned the difficulty of the matter; the folk excused him and left, but Ibn Abbas pressed him. By Allah, he found no escape from fulfilling our need. We left until we entered the mosque, where the folk were in circles. Hassan said: I laughed as I heard them; by Allah, he was the most deserving of it; by Allah, it is the remnant of prophethood, the inheritance of Ahmad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the refinement of his lineages and the extraction of the likeness of his natures. The folk said: Be fair, O Hassan. Ibn Abbas said: They spoke truth. Hassan began praising Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) saying: Kahaman Khabla. The governor said: By Allah, by al-kaham al-khabl he meant none but me; Allah is between me and him."
"3593","349 - Hassan ibn Shaddad al-Tuhawi of Banu Tuhayyah. 3594 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Sahl Abu Sahl al-Basri: Yaqub ibn Udaydah ibn Affas ibn Hassan ibn Shaddad ibn Shihab ibn Zuhayr ibn Rabiah ibn Abi Sud al-Tuhawi narrated: my father Udaydah narrated to me from his father Affas from his grandfather Hassan ibn Shaddad: his mother came as a delegate to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to you that you supplicate for this son of mine that Allah make blessing in him for him and make him abundant and good. He performed ablution from the remainder of his ablution water, wiped his face and said: O Allah, bless him in him and make him abundant and good."
"3594","350 - Hassan ibn Abi Jabir al-Sulami. 3595 - Narrated al-Hadrami, and Musa ibn Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated, both saying: Dawud ibn Rashid narrated: Baqiyyah narrated from Saeed ibn Ibrahim: Abu Yusuf narrated to me, saying: I heard Hassan ibn Abi Jabir al-Sulami say: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Taif and he saw men of his Companions who had dyed their beards red and yellow. He said: Welcome to those who dye yellow and red."
"3595","351 - Hubab ibn Amr al-Ansari, brother of Abu al-Yasar. 3596 - Narrated Ali ibn Saeed al-Razi from Muhammad ibn Humayd: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated: Ibn Ishaq narrated from al-Khattab ibn Salih from his mother from Sallamah bint Maqil, who said: I belonged to Hubab ibn Amr and he died leaving me a child of his. His wife said: Now you will be sold for his debt. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: Who holds the estate of Hubab? He said: His brother Abu al-Yasar Kab ibn Amr. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: Do not sell her; free her, and when you hear captives have come to me, come to me and I will compensate you. They did so; after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they differed among themselves: some said the umm al-walad is owned - else the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not have compensated them; others said she is free, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed her."
"3596","352 - Hubab ibn al-Mundhir al-Ansari. 3597 - Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Mamar from al-Zuhri: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that the one who said: I am Judhayluha al-muhakkak and Udhayquha al-murajjab, was Hubab ibn al-Mundhir."
"3597","353 - Hubab Abu Aqil al-Ansari, and it is said: son of Abu Aqil Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Thalabah. 3598 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated: Khalid ibn Yasar narrated to me from Ibn Abi Aqil from his father: he spent the night dragging the rope on his back for two sa of dates; he turned with one to his family for their use and came with the other seeking nearness to Allah, mighty and majestic. He brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Scatter it among the charity. The hypocrites spoke of him and mocked: this one had no need to seek nearness to Allah with a sa of dates. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: Those who scoff at the voluntary givers among the believers in charities and those who find only their effort, to the end of the two verses."
"3598","354 - Humam al-Aslami. 3599 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Sufyan ibn Waki from his father: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated from Mamar from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Yazid ibn Nuaym: a man of Aslam called Ubayd ibn Uwaymir lay with his slave-girl; she bore him a boy called Humam, in the Jahiliyyah. My uncle came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spoke to him about his son. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Take your son as you can. He went and took his son, bringing him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The boy's master came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who offered him two boys, saying: Take one and leave the man his son. He took a boy and left him his son."
"3599","355 - Hazn ibn Abi Wahb al-Makhzumi. 3600 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Hudbah ibn Khalid: Hammam narrated from Qatadah from Saeed ibn al-Musayyib: his grandfather came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said to him: What is your name? He said: Hazn (Rough). He wanted to change his name, but he said: I would not change a name my father gave me. Saeed said: That roughness remains in us to this hour."
"3600","356 - Hawt ibn Yazid al-Ansari. 3601 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil narrated: Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd narrated: al-Harith ibn Ziyad al-Saidi narrated to me that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Khandaq while he pledged people upon emigration. He said: O Messenger of Allah, pledge this one upon emigration. He said: Who is this? He said: My cousin Hawt ibn Yazid, or Yazid ibn Hawt. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not pledge you; people emigrate to you while you do not emigrate to them."
